#: manual/design/cli.md:81
msgid "No `run` command: benchmarks are MoonBit code and are run with `moon test` or `moon run` of your own package."
msgstr "没有 `run` 命令：基准测试是 MoonBit 代码，通过对你自己的包执行 `moon test` 或 `moon run` 来运行。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:83
msgid "`--open` uses the macOS `open` command."
msgstr "`--open` 使用 macOS 的 `open` 命令。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:84
msgid "`replay` reads files only, executes the first failure only, and passes the command directly to the process API (no shell)."
msgstr "`replay` 只读取文件，只执行第一个失败，并把命令直接传给进程 API（不经过 shell）。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:86
msgid "The version string is fixed in the source."
msgstr "版本字符串在源码中固定。"

#: manual/design/event.md:1
msgid "event design"
msgstr "event 设计"

#: manual/design/event.md:5
msgid "The event stream is the audit record of an experiment: every number in a report and every replayed failure must be recoverable from it. `event` keeps that record append-only and line-oriented, and keeps storage choices out of the runner."
msgstr "事件流是实验的审计记录：报告中的每个数字和每个被重放的失败都必须能从中恢复。`event` 让这份记录保持只追加、面向行，并让存储方面的选择远离运行器。"

#: manual/design/event.md:12
msgid "The record must be streamable, appendable and readable by any tool."
msgstr "记录必须可流式处理、可追加，并能被任何工具读取。"

#: manual/design/event.md:13
msgid "JSON numbers are doubles, so 64-bit integers cannot be stored as numbers."
msgstr "JSON 数字是双精度浮点数，因此 64 位整数无法以数字形式存储。"

#: manual/design/event.md:14
msgid "The package does no file IO, so it runs on every target."
msgstr "该包不做文件 IO，因此能在每个目标上运行。"

#: manual/design/event.md:18
msgid "Model a run as a sequence of events $e_1, e_2, \\dots, e_N$ and a sink as a fold $s_{k} = \\text{emit}(s_{k-1}, e_k)$. JSONL serialization is a map $J$ from events to lines, and the stored stream is the lines $J(e_1), \\dots, J(e_N)$ joined by newlines."
msgstr "把一次运行建模为事件序列 $e_1, e_2, \\dots, e_N$，把接收器建模为折叠 $s_{k} = \\text{emit}(s_{k-1}, e_k)$。JSONL 序列化是从事件到行的映射 $J$，存储的流是用换行符连接的各行 $J(e_1), \\dots, J(e_N)$。"

#: manual/design/event.md:23
msgid "Two properties follow from this shape."
msgstr "这种形状带来两个性质。"

#: manual/design/event.md:25
msgid "**Prefix closure.** Every prefix of complete lines is the valid record of $e_1, \\dots, e_k$. A crash after $k$ events leaves such a prefix (without the final summary event, which the runner emits last); a reader that processes lines independently can use it."
msgstr "**前缀封闭。** 由完整行组成的每个前缀都是 $e_1, \\dots, e_k$ 的有效记录。在 $k$ 个事件后崩溃会留下这样一个前缀（不含 runner 最后发出的汇总事件）；独立处理各行的读取器可以使用它。"

#: manual/design/event.md:29
msgid "**Projection commutes with concatenation.** A report is built line by line, so the projection of two concatenated streams is computed from the projections of their lines. Merging or filtering streams is plain text processing."
msgstr "**投影与拼接可交换。** 报告是逐行构建的，因此两个拼接起来的流的投影可以由各行的投影算出。合并或过滤流只是普通的文本处理。"

#: manual/design/event.md:34
msgid "`tee` is the product of two folds: it maps $(s, t)$ to $(\\text{emit}_1(s, e), \\text{emit}_2(t, e))$, so a run can be stored in memory and on disk with one pass."
msgstr "`tee` 是两个折叠的积：它把 $(s, t)$ 映射到 $(\\text{emit}_1(s, e), \\text{emit}_2(t, e))$，因此一次运行可以在单趟中同时存储到内存和磁盘。"

#: manual/design/event.md:40
msgid "A record of closures"
msgstr "由闭包组成的记录"

#: manual/design/event.md:42
msgid "*Problem.* Sinks keep state (arrays, file handles) and are combined (`tee`). *Options.* A trait with methods; a record of functions. *Choice.* A record of five closures. *Why.* Closures capture whatever state a sink needs, a record can be built inline in a test, and combinators like `tee` are ordinary functions that return a new record."
msgstr "*问题。* 接收器持有状态（数组、文件句柄）并且会被组合（`tee`）。*方案。* 带方法的 trait；由函数组成的记录。*选择。* 由五个闭包组成的记录。*理由。* 闭包可以捕获接收器所需的任何状态，记录可以在测试中内联构建，而 `tee` 这样的组合子就是返回新记录的普通函数。"

#: manual/design/event.md:48
msgid "One JSON object per line"
msgstr "每行一个 JSON 对象"

#: manual/design/event.md:50
msgid "*Problem.* The record must be streamable, appendable and readable by any tool. *Choice.* JSONL with a `type` discriminator and an `artifact_version` on every line. *Why.* A line is self-describing, so readers can skip types they do not know, grep works, and a crash never corrupts earlier lines. The version on each line allows streams from different versions to be concatenated and still rejected precisely."
msgstr "*问题。* 记录必须可流式传输、可追加，并且能被任何工具读取。*选择。* 采用 JSONL，每一行都带有 `type` 判别字段和 `artifact_version`。*理由。* 每一行都是自描述的，因此读取器可以跳过不认识的类型，grep 也能用，崩溃也永远不会损坏之前的行。每行带版本使来自不同版本的流可以拼接在一起，同时仍能被精确拒绝。"

#: manual/design/event.md:57
msgid "Raw values only"
msgstr "只记录原始值"

#: manual/design/event.md:59
msgid "Observations carry the per-iteration time of one batch, never a mean, median or filtered value. Every statistic in a report is recomputed from these raw values, and an outlier policy cannot rewrite history."
msgstr "观测携带的是一个批次的每次迭代时间，从不是均值、中位数或过滤后的值。报告中的每个统计量都从这些原始值重新计算，离群值策略无法改写历史。"

#: manual/design/event.md:63
msgid "Seeds as strings"
msgstr "种子写为字符串"

#: manual/design/event.md:65
msgid "`seed` is written as a decimal string, because a JSON number is a double and cannot represent every 64-bit integer: integers above $2^{53}$ would be rounded."
msgstr "`seed` 写为十进制字符串，因为 JSON 数值是双精度浮点数，无法表示每个 64 位整数：大于 $2^{53}$ 的整数会被舍入。"

#: manual/design/event.md:68
msgid "Finish returns a location"
msgstr "finish 返回位置"

#: manual/design/event.md:70
msgid "`finish` returns where the record went (`memory://run/…`, `jsonl://memory/…`, a file name), and the runner stores it in the summary. The caller learns where the evidence is without the runner knowing about files."
msgstr "`finish` 返回记录的去向（`memory://run/…`、`jsonl://memory/…`、一个文件名），运行器把它存入摘要。调用者无需运行器了解文件，就能知道证据在哪里。"

#: manual/design/event.md:76
msgid "Each emit call writes exactly one line (`JsonlSink`, `streaming_jsonl`) or appends exactly one element (`InMemorySink`)."
msgstr "每次 emit 调用恰好写出一行（`JsonlSink`、`streaming_jsonl`）或恰好追加一个元素（`InMemorySink`）。"

#: manual/design/event.md:78
msgid "Every line carries `artifact_version` `mmka_1` and a `type`."
msgstr "每一行都带有 `artifact_version` `mmka_1` 和 `type`。"

#: manual/design/event.md:79
msgid "`tee` preserves order: for every event, the left sink sees it before the right sink."
msgstr "`tee` 保持顺序：对每个事件，左侧接收器都先于右侧接收器看到它。"

#: manual/design/event.md:81
msgid ""
"`to_jsonl` has one line per event, separated by `\\n"
"`."
msgstr ""
"`to_jsonl` 每个事件一行，以 `\\n"
"` 分隔。"

#: manual/design/event.md:82
msgid "Strings are escaped by the JSON encoder, so a line never contains a raw newline."
msgstr "字符串由 JSON 编码器转义，因此一行中永远不会包含原始换行符。"

#: manual/design/event.md:87
msgid "**A single JSON document per run.** Not appendable; a crash loses everything."
msgstr "**每次运行一个 JSON 文档。** 不可追加；一次崩溃会丢失全部内容。"

#: manual/design/event.md:89
msgid "**CSV.** Nested evidence (operands, flags, environment) does not fit."
msgstr "**CSV。** 嵌套的证据（操作数、标志、环境）放不进去。"

#: manual/design/event.md:90
msgid "**Binary formats.** Unreadable in review and in issue reports."
msgstr "**二进制格式。** 在评审和 issue 报告中无法阅读。"

#: manual/design/event.md:94
msgid "No file IO: writing lines to disk is the caller's job (the `cli` and applications do it)."
msgstr "没有文件 IO：把行写入磁盘是调用者的工作（由 `cli` 和应用完成）。"

#: manual/design/event.md:96
msgid "`InMemorySink` does not keep the summary."
msgstr "`InMemorySink` 不保存摘要。"

#: manual/design/event.md:97
msgid "No reader lives here; `report` and `cli` parse the stream."
msgstr "这里没有读取器；由 `report` 和 `cli` 解析事件流。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:1
msgid "experiment design"
msgstr "experiment 设计"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:5
msgid "A benchmark compares implementations that are supposed to compute the same thing. `experiment` states what \"the same\" means (oracles), makes a failure small enough to debug (shrinking), and decides when a size-dependent preference is strong enough to become a deployment rule (crossover analysis). Everything is a pure function of explicit inputs."
msgstr "基准测试比较的是本应计算同一事物的多个实现。`experiment` 阐明“同一”的含义（判定器），把失败缩小到便于调试的程度（缩减），并判断随规模变化的偏好何时强到足以成为部署规则（交叉点分析）。一切都是显式输入的纯函数。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:13
msgid "Correctness is case-specific: tolerances, flags, traps and accepted deviations differ between cases."
msgstr "正确性因用例而异：容差、标志、陷阱和可接受的偏差在不同用例之间各不相同。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:15
msgid "One oracle evaluation may run a whole operation sequence, so every search over inputs needs a budget."
msgstr "一次预言机求值可能运行整个操作序列，因此对输入的每次搜索都需要预算。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:17
msgid "A deployment rule must not claim anything about scales that were not measured."
msgstr "部署规则不得对未测量过的规模做出任何断言。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:22
msgid "Oracles as relations"
msgstr "作为关系的判定器"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:24
msgid "For an input $x$ and step $k$, a reference oracle defines an expected outcome $e_k(x)$ and a judgement $V(x, k, e, a) \\in \\text{ValidationStatus}$ for the actual outcome $a$. Equality is the special case $V = \\text{Valid} \\iff a = e$; floating-point code usually needs a tolerance $\\lvert a - e\\rvert \\le \\epsilon$, and IEEE-aware code compares flags as well."
msgstr "对于输入 $x$ 和第 $k$ 步，参考判定器定义一个期望结果 $e_k(x)$，以及针对实际结果 $a$ 的判断 $V(x, k, e, a) \\in \\text{ValidationStatus}$。相等是特例 $V = \\text{Valid} \\iff a = e$；浮点代码通常需要容差 $\\lvert a - e\\rvert \\le \\epsilon$，而感知 IEEE 的代码还要比较标志。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:30
msgid "A relational oracle judges a pair of implementations, $R(x, k, a^{(i)}, a^{(j)})$. It does not need a reference, but it only detects disagreement: if all implementations share a bug, the relation holds. The runner checks all $\\binom{m}{2}$ unordered pairs of $m$ implementations; when the relation is an equivalence (for example exact equality of results), the pairs are redundant but cheap, and a single deviating implementation shows up in $m-1$ pairs, which makes it easy to identify."
msgstr "关系判定器判定一对实现，$R(x, k, a^{(i)}, a^{(j)})$。它不需要参考，但只能检测出分歧：如果所有实现都有同一个缺陷，关系仍然成立。运行器检查 $m$ 个实现的全部 $\\binom{m}{2}$ 个无序对；当关系是等价关系（例如结果完全相等）时，这些配对虽有冗余但代价低廉，而单个偏离的实现会出现在 $m-1$ 个配对中，因此很容易被识别出来。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:38
msgid "Shrinking as greedy descent"
msgstr "作为贪心下降的缩减"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:40
msgid "Let $C(x)$ be the candidates of $x$ and $P$ the failure predicate. `shrink` computes"
msgstr "设 $C(x)$ 为 $x$ 的候选，$P$ 为失败谓词。`shrink` 计算"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:47
msgid "and stops when no candidate satisfies $P$ or after `max_steps` evaluations of $P$."
msgstr "并在没有候选满足 $P$ 时，或在对 $P$ 求值 `max_steps` 次之后停止。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:50
msgid "**Termination.** Every iteration of the inner loop evaluates $P$ once and increments a counter; the outer loop stops when the counter reaches `max_steps` or an iteration accepts nothing. At most `max_steps` evaluations happen, even when $C$ is cyclic."
msgstr "**终止性。** 内层循环的每次迭代对 $P$ 求值一次并使计数器加一；当计数器达到 `max_steps` 或某次迭代什么也没接受时，外层循环停止。即使 $C$ 有环，最多也只发生 `max_steps` 次求值。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:54
msgid "**Invariant.** If $P(x_0)$ holds, then $P(x_j)$ holds for every accepted $x_j$, because a candidate is accepted only when $P$ holds for it. The result is therefore still a failing input. (`shrink` does not test $x_0$ itself.)"
msgstr "**不变量。** 若 $P(x_0)$ 成立，则对每个被接受的 $x_j$，$P(x_j)$ 都成立，因为只有当 $P$ 对某个候选成立时它才会被接受。因此结果仍然是一个失败的输入。（`shrink` 不测试 $x_0$ 本身。）"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:57
msgid "**Local minimality.** If the loop stops because no candidate fails, the result is a local minimum: no element of $C(\\text{result})$ satisfies $P$. If it stops because of the budget, it may not be."
msgstr "**局部极小性。** 如果循环因没有候选失败而停止，结果就是一个局部极小：$C(\\text{result})$ 中没有元素满足 $P$。如果因预算耗尽而停止，则未必如此。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:61
msgid "With $C(n) = [\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor, n-1]$ and a threshold predicate $P(n) = (n \\ge t)$, the descent halves while it can and then steps down by one, reaching exactly $t$ in $O(\\log n + t)$ accepted steps."
msgstr "取 $C(n) = [\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor, n-1]$ 和阈值谓词 $P(n) = (n \\ge t)$，下降过程在可以时减半，然后逐一递减，在 $O(\\log n + t)$ 个被接受的步骤内恰好到达 $t$。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:65
msgid "Crossover detection"
msgstr "交叉点检测"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:67
msgid "Let $s_1 < s_2 < \\dots < s_N$ be sorted scales and $\\ell_i \\in \\{A, B, \\text{Unknown}\\}$ the verdict at $s_i$. The number of transitions is"
msgstr "设 $s_1 < s_2 < \\dots < s_N$ 为排好序的规模，$\\ell_i \\in \\{A, B, \\text{Unknown}\\}$ 为 $s_i$ 处的判定结果。转变的次数为"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:74
msgid "If the relative delta $r(s)$ is monotone in the scale, the labels $\\text{label}(r(s_i))$ form a monotone sequence $A \\dots A\\, U \\dots U\\, B \\dots B$ (or the reverse), so a well-behaved preference has at most one transition. $T = 1$ yields the boundary $(s_{i-1}, s_i)$ of the unique transition; $T > 1$ means the preference flips more than once and cannot be expressed as one threshold; $T = 0$ means no adjacent pair of definite, different labels."
msgstr "如果相对差值 $r(s)$ 关于规模单调，则标签 $\\text{label}(r(s_i))$ 构成单调序列 $A \\dots A\\, U \\dots U\\, B \\dots B$（或其逆序），因此表现良好的偏好至多有一次转变。$T = 1$ 给出唯一那次转变的分界 $(s_{i-1}, s_i)$；$T > 1$ 意味着偏好翻转了不止一次，无法用单个阈值表达；$T = 0$ 意味着不存在一对相邻的、确定且不同的标签。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:81
msgid "`comparator_label(r, t)` maps the relative delta to the labels with the same threshold rule as `stats`: $A$ if $r < 0$ and $r \\le -t$, $B$ if $r > 0$ and $r \\ge t$, `Unknown` otherwise. The `Unknown` band $(-t, t)$ keeps noise around $r = 0$ from creating spurious transitions; for $t = 0$ it shrinks to the single point $r = 0$, so an exact tie never counts as a preference. A threshold that is `NaN`, infinite or negative has no band at all and yields `Unknown` for every $r$ (and so $T = 0$); `runner.validate_protocol` rejects such thresholds before a run."
msgstr "`comparator_label(r, t)` 用与 `stats` 相同的阈值规则把相对差值映射为标签：$r < 0$ 且 $r \\le -t$ 为 $A$，$r > 0$ 且 $r \\ge t$ 为 $B$，否则为 `Unknown`。`Unknown` 带 $(-t, t)$ 可以防止 $r = 0$ 附近的噪声产生虚假的转变；当 $t = 0$ 时它收缩为单点 $r = 0$，因此完全持平永远不算作偏好。为 `NaN`、无穷大或负数的阈值根本没有这条带，对每个 $r$ 都给出 `Unknown`（因此 $T = 0$）；`runner.validate_protocol` 会在运行前拒绝这样的阈值。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:90
msgid "The labels are counted in scale order. `crossover_from_labels` first sorts the pairs $(s_i, \\ell_i)$ stably with `ScaleDomain.compare`, so the sequence above is defined by the comparator and not by the order in which the caller listed the scales. Without the sort, a single crossover measured in the order $64, 16, 256$ with labels $B, A, B$ would count two transitions."
msgstr "标签按规模顺序计数。`crossover_from_labels` 先用 `ScaleDomain.compare` 对 $(s_i, \\ell_i)$ 对进行稳定排序，因此上面的序列由比较函数决定，而不是由调用者列出规模的顺序决定。如果不排序，按 $64, 16, 256$ 的顺序测得、标签为 $B, A, B$ 的单个交叉点会被计为两次转变。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:98
msgid "Oracles are values"
msgstr "判定器是值"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:100
msgid "*Problem.* Each case needs its own notion of correctness. *Choice.* Oracles are records of functions with an id. *Why.* They can capture tolerances and contexts, are named in every validation event, and can be built inline."
msgstr "*问题。* 每个用例都需要自己的正确性概念。*选择。* 判定器是带 id 的函数记录。*理由。* 它们可以捕获容差和上下文，在每个验证事件中都有名字，并且可以内联构建。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:104
msgid "Outcomes, not just values, reach the oracle"
msgstr "到达判定器的是结果，而不只是值"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:106
msgid "The oracle sees `ExecutionOutcome`s, so it can accept a documented `ExpectedDifference`, compare raised flags, or require that both sides trap. The runner pre-classifies worker crashes, timeouts, decoding errors and `Unsupported` before the oracle is called, so oracles only judge real results."
msgstr "判定器看到的是 `ExecutionOutcome`，因此它可以接受有文档记录的 `ExpectedDifference`、比较引发的标志，或者要求两侧都触发陷阱。运行器在调用判定器之前会预先分类工作进程崩溃、超时、解码错误和 `Unsupported`，因此判定器只判定真实的结果。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:111
msgid "Greedy, first-improvement shrinking"
msgstr "贪心的首次改进式缩减"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:113
msgid "*Options.* Exhaustive search for the smallest failing input; delta debugging; greedy descent. *Choice.* Greedy descent with an explicit candidate function and an evaluation budget. *Why.* Each evaluation may run a whole operation sequence, so the budget is what bounds the cost; the candidate function lets the user encode the structure of the input (halve a size, drop an element). The accepted path is recorded so a reader can see how the counterexample was reached."
msgstr "*方案。* 穷举搜索最小的失败输入；delta 调试；贪心下降。*选择。* 带显式候选函数和求值预算的贪心下降。*理由。* 每次求值都可能运行完整的操作序列，因此真正限制代价的是预算；候选函数让用户编码输入的结构（把规模减半、删除一个元素）。被接受的路径会被记录下来，读者可以看到反例是如何得到的。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:121
msgid "Conservative crossover"
msgstr "保守的交叉点"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:123
msgid "*Problem.* A crossover becomes a deployment rule (`DeploymentPolicy::Piecewise`) that will be applied to inputs never measured. *Choice.* Accept a boundary only for exactly one transition; report `NonMonotonic` otherwise and leave the policy to the user. *Why.* A rule built from a noisy, flipping preference would encode noise."
msgstr "*问题。* 交叉点会成为部署规则（`DeploymentPolicy::Piecewise`），并被应用于从未测量过的输入。*选择。* 只有恰好一次转变时才接受分界；否则报告 `NonMonotonic`，把策略留给用户。*理由。* 基于嘈杂、反复翻转的偏好建立的规则只会编码噪声。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:131
msgid "`shrink` evaluates the predicate at most `max_steps` times and returns an input satisfying it whenever the initial input does."
msgstr "`shrink` 最多对谓词求值 `max_steps` 次，并且只要初始输入满足谓词，就返回一个满足它的输入。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:133
msgid "`crossover_from_labels` returns `Found` only when there is exactly one transition, and its boundary consists of the two adjacent scales of that transition."
msgstr "只有恰好存在一次转变时，`crossover_from_labels` 才返回 `Found`，其分界由该次转变的两个相邻规模组成。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:136
msgid "`ReferenceOracle::equal` returns `Valid` only for two `Value` outcomes accepted by the comparator."
msgstr "只有当两个结果都是 `Value` 且被比较器接受时，`ReferenceOracle::equal` 才返回 `Valid`。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:138
msgid "For a finite $t \\ge 0$, `comparator_label` partitions the real line into $(-\\infty, -t] \\setminus \\{0\\}$ (`A`), $[t, \\infty) \\setminus \\{0\\}$ (`B`) and the rest (`Unknown`); for any other $t$ every label is `Unknown`."
msgstr "对于有限的 $t \\ge 0$，`comparator_label` 把实数轴划分为 $(-\\infty, -t] \\setminus \\{0\\}$（`A`）、$[t, \\infty) \\setminus \\{0\\}$（`B`）和其余部分（`Unknown`）；对于其他任何 $t$，每个标签都是 `Unknown`。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:141
msgid "`crossover_from_labels` depends only on the multiset of (scale, label) pairs and the comparator, except for the order of pairs whose scales compare equal, which the stable sort keeps."
msgstr "`crossover_from_labels` 只依赖于（规模, 标签）对的多重集和比较函数，唯一的例外是规模比较相等的那些对的顺序，稳定排序会保留它。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:147
msgid "**Statistical change-point detection on raw timings.** Needs a noise model; labels from practical thresholds are explainable."
msgstr "**在原始计时上做统计变点检测。** 需要噪声模型；而基于实际阈值的标签是可解释的。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:149
msgid "**Interpolating the boundary.** The scales between two measured ones were not measured; the result names the two measured scales instead."
msgstr "**对分界进行插值。** 两个测量规模之间的规模并未被测量；结果改为给出那两个测量过的规模。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:151
msgid "**Delta debugging.** Powerful for sequences, but needs a fixed input representation; the candidate function is more general."
msgstr "**delta 调试。** 对序列很强大，但需要固定的输入表示；候选函数更通用。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:156
msgid "`crossover_from_labels` uses `ScaleDomain.compare` only to sort; equal scales are not merged, and their labels stay in input order."
msgstr "`crossover_from_labels` 只用 `ScaleDomain.compare` 来排序；相等的规模不会被合并，它们的标签保持输入顺序。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:158
msgid "A transition across an `Unknown` label (A, Unknown, B) is not counted, so such a sequence reports `NoCrossover`."
msgstr "跨越 `Unknown` 标签的转变（A、Unknown、B）不计数，因此这样的序列报告 `NoCrossover`。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:160
msgid "Oracles are not run here; the runner runs them. For each input selected for reference validation, the runner evaluates `ReferenceOracle.sequence_length` once. The result must be positive and equal the case's configured sequence length; otherwise the run raises `RunConfigError` before candidate execution. This equality is a correctness precondition: checking only the common prefix would leave a suffix without a verdict. If an expected or actual operation sequence terminates early, the runner emits an `Invalid` validation for the length mismatch after validating the common steps."
msgstr "判定器不在这里运行；由运行器运行它们。对于每个需要进行参考验证的输入，运行器会计算一次 `ReferenceOracle.sequence_length`。结果必须为正，并且等于用例配置的序列长度；否则运行器会在候选执行前抛出 `RunConfigError`。长度相等是正确性前提：如果只检查共有前缀，剩余后缀就没有判定结果。若期望操作序列或实际操作序列提前终止，运行器会先验证共有步骤，然后针对长度不匹配生成一条 `Invalid` 验证。"

#: manual/design/experiment.md:168
msgid "`shrink` does not check that the initial input fails."
msgstr "`shrink` 不检查初始输入是否失败。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:1
msgid "fixture design"
msgstr "fixture 设计"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:5
msgid "The same input must reach every implementation, and the cost of setting it up must be either inside or outside the measurement by declaration, not by accident. `fixture` separates the five things that happen to an input (generate, identify, copy, prepare, reset) so that the runner can place each of them on the right side of the clock."
msgstr "同一个输入必须到达每个实现，而准备它的代价是否计入测量，必须由声明决定，而不是出于偶然。`fixture` 把发生在输入上的五件事（生成、标识、复制、准备、重置）分开，使运行器能把每一件都放在时钟的正确一侧。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:13
msgid "Input, prepared and output types are arbitrary, so the lifecycle is generic in them."
msgstr "输入、准备后的值和输出的类型是任意的，因此生命周期对它们是泛型的。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:15
msgid "The runner must know on which side of the clock each step falls."
msgstr "runner 必须知道每一步落在计时的哪一侧。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:16
msgid "Fixtures are often written inline in a test, next to the case they serve."
msgstr "fixture 常常直接内联写在测试中，紧挨着它所服务的用例。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:20
msgid "A fixture is a small state machine applied per dataset $D$ and implementation $I$:"
msgstr "夹具是一个按数据集 $D$ 和实现 $I$ 应用的小型状态机："

#: manual/design/fixture.md:31
msgid "Two equations express the contract the runner relies on."
msgstr "两个等式表达了运行器所依赖的契约。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:33
msgid "**Isolation.** If an implementation mutates $p$, the next preparation must still see the original $x$: $\\text{prepare}(\\text{clone}(x))$ must not share mutable state with $x$. Then every batch starts from the same state, and the measured workload is the same function of $x$ in every block."
msgstr "**隔离。** 如果某个实现修改了 $p$，下一次准备仍必须看到原始的 $x$：$\\text{prepare}(\\text{clone}(x))$ 不得与 $x$ 共享可变状态。这样每个批次都从相同的状态开始，并且在每个区组中被测量的工作负载都是 $x$ 的同一个函数。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:37
msgid "**Determinism.** $\\text{materialize}$ is a function of the context alone, so equal contexts give equal inputs and equal fingerprints: $\\text{ctx} = \\text{ctx}' \\Rightarrow \\text{fingerprint}(\\text{materialize}(\\text{ctx})) = \\text{fingerprint}(\\text{materialize}(\\text{ctx}'))$."
msgstr "**确定性。** $\\text{materialize}$ 只是上下文的函数，因此相等的上下文给出相等的输入和相等的指纹：$\\text{ctx} = \\text{ctx}' \\Rightarrow \\text{fingerprint}(\\text{materialize}(\\text{ctx})) = \\text{fingerprint}(\\text{materialize}(\\text{ctx}'))$。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:41
msgid "The runner checks neither; violating them makes blocks measure different workloads."
msgstr "运行器对两者都不检查；违反它们会使各区组测量不同的工作负载。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:44
msgid "Setup cost in the measurement"
msgstr "测量中的准备代价"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:46
msgid "Let one operation cost $c$ and one preparation $a$. For a batch of $n$ operations the runner reports $\\hat T / n$, where"
msgstr "设一次操作的代价为 $c$，一次准备的代价为 $a$。对于含 $n$ 次操作的批次，运行器报告 $\\hat T / n$，其中"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:53
msgid "long-lived"
msgstr "长期存活"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:53
msgid "$c$ (the one preparation lands in the first warmup batch, or the first calibration batch without warmup; neither is reported as an observation)"
msgstr "$c$（那一次准备落在第一个预热批次中；没有预热时落在第一个校准批次中；两者都不会作为观测值报告）"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:55
msgid "Including setup per batch measures an amortized cost that depends on the batch size chosen by calibration; include it only per iteration, or when the batch size is fixed."
msgstr "按批次计入准备工作，测得的是取决于校准所选批次大小的摊销代价；只有按迭代计入，或批次大小固定时，才应计入准备工作。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:61
msgid "Closures in a record, not a trait"
msgstr "记录中的闭包，而不是 trait"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:63
msgid "*Problem.* Fixtures differ in input type, prepared type and policy, and are often written inline in a test. *Choice.* `Fixture` is a record of functions with three type parameters. *Why.* A trait would need one type per fixture and could not carry an id, a version and a policy as values."
msgstr "*问题。* 各夹具的输入类型、准备后类型和策略各不相同，而且常常在测试中内联编写。*选择。* `Fixture` 是带三个类型参数的函数记录。*理由。* trait 需要为每个夹具定义一个类型，并且无法把 id、版本和策略作为值携带。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:68
msgid "Clone before prepare"
msgstr "先克隆再准备"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:70
msgid "The runner always calls `clone_input` before `prepare`. `Fixture::immutable` makes both the identity, which is free for values that are never mutated; a mutable input supplies a real copy. Keeping clone and prepare apart lets a fixture copy the input once and build a workspace around it, and makes the cost of each visible."
msgstr "运行器总是在 `prepare` 之前调用 `clone_input`。`Fixture::immutable` 让两者都成为恒等函数，这对永不修改的值没有代价；可变输入则提供真正的副本。把克隆和准备分开，使夹具可以只复制一次输入并围绕它建立工作区，也使两者各自的代价都可见。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:76
msgid "Implementation-aware preparation"
msgstr "感知实现的准备"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:78
msgid "`prepare` receives the implementation id, so it can produce the layout an implementation expects (packed, transposed, padded). The preparation is then part of the fixture, and its timing follows the declared policy rather than hiding inside one implementation's payload."
msgstr "`prepare` 接收实现 id，因此它可以生成某个实现所期望的布局（打包、转置、填充）。这样准备工作就属于夹具，其计时遵循声明的策略，而不是隐藏在某个实现的负载中。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:83
msgid "Policy as data"
msgstr "策略即数据"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:85
msgid "`SetupPolicy` is recorded with every observation (`setup_timing`) and in the event stream. A reader can tell a cold-start measurement from a warm one without reading code."
msgstr "`SetupPolicy` 随每个观测（`setup_timing`）以及在事件流中被记录。读者无需阅读代码就能区分冷启动测量和热态测量。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:91
msgid "`materialize` and `fingerprint` run once per dataset."
msgstr "`materialize` 和 `fingerprint` 对每个数据集运行一次。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:92
msgid "`prepare` always receives a fresh `clone_input` result."
msgstr "`prepare` 总是接收一个新的 `clone_input` 结果。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:93
msgid "Every short-lived prepared value is reset exactly once; long-lived values are reset at the runner's checkpoints and reused (see the [runner design](runner.md))."
msgstr "每个短期存活的准备值都恰好被重置一次；长期存活的值在运行器的检查点处被重置并复用（参见 [runner 设计](runner.md)）。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:96
msgid "`Fixture::immutable` uses identity functions and a no-op reset."
msgstr "`Fixture::immutable` 使用恒等函数和空操作的重置。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:100
msgid "**Letting implementations copy their own input.** The copy would be timed for some implementations and not for others."
msgstr "**让实现自行复制输入。** 这样复制在某些实现中会被计时，而在另一些实现中不会。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:102
msgid "**One setup hook.** Could not distinguish generation (once per dataset) from preparation (per batch or iteration)."
msgstr "**单一的准备钩子。** 无法区分生成（每个数据集一次）与准备（每个批次或每次迭代）。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:107
msgid "The fixture does not enforce isolation or determinism; it states the contract."
msgstr "夹具并不强制隔离性或确定性；它只陈述契约。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:109
msgid "`WorkspaceScope` is descriptive; the runner keys its cache per implementation and dataset."
msgstr "`WorkspaceScope` 是描述性的；运行器按实现和数据集为其缓存建立键。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:111
msgid "`PerRun` and `PerDataset` are prepared per implementation, like `PerImplementation`."
msgstr "`PerRun` 和 `PerDataset` 与 `PerImplementation` 一样，按实现分别准备。"

#: manual/design/fixture.md:113
msgid "The fixture does not measure memory."
msgstr "夹具不测量内存。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:1
msgid "generator design"
msgstr "generator 设计"

#: manual/design/generator.md:5
msgid "A benchmark must be rerunnable on the same inputs years later and on another target. `generator` provides the two primitives this needs: a seed derivation that turns one run seed into independent, named streams, and a fingerprint that records which input was actually used. Both are pure functions of their arguments."
msgstr "基准测试必须能在多年以后、在另一个目标上以相同的输入重新运行。`generator` 提供为此所需的两个基本组件：一种把一个运行种子转化为相互独立的具名流的种子派生方法，以及一个记录实际所用输入的指纹。两者都是其参数的纯函数。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:13
msgid "Derived seeds and fingerprints must be bit-identical on native, JS, wasm and wasm-gc, years apart."
msgstr "派生的种子和指纹必须在 native、JS、wasm 和 wasm-gc 上逐位相同，即使相隔多年。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:15
msgid "Inputs must depend on their names and ids only, never on the order in which they are generated."
msgstr "输入只能依赖于它们的名称和 id，绝不依赖于生成它们的顺序。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:17
msgid "The functions keep no state between calls."
msgstr "这些函数在调用之间不保留任何状态。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:21
msgid "All arithmetic is on 64-bit words, modulo $2^{64}$. Write $\\oplus$ for exclusive or and $\\gg$ for a logical right shift."
msgstr "所有算术都在 64 位字上进行，模 $2^{64}$。用 $\\oplus$ 表示异或，用 $\\gg$ 表示逻辑右移。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:24
msgid "The derivation"
msgstr "派生过程"

#: manual/design/generator.md:26
msgid "`derive_seed(s, D, i)` with a domain string $D = c_1 c_2 \\dots c_m$ (Unicode code points) and an index $i$ computes"
msgstr "对域字符串 $D = c_1 c_2 \\dots c_m$（Unicode 码点）和索引 $i$，`derive_seed(s, D, i)` 计算"

#: manual/design/generator.md:40
msgid "The first two lines are FNV-1a with the 64-bit offset basis and prime, keyed by the seed; the third multiplies by $\\lfloor 2^{64}/\\varphi\\rfloor$, the golden ratio increment of SplitMix64; the last three are the SplitMix64 output finalizer.[^splitmix]"
msgstr "前两行是以种子为密钥、使用 64 位偏移基和素数的 FNV-1a；第三行乘以 $\\lfloor 2^{64}/\\varphi\\rfloor$，即 SplitMix64 的黄金比例增量；最后三行是 SplitMix64 的输出终结器。[^splitmix]"

#: manual/design/generator.md:45
msgid "G. L. Steele, D. Lea and C. H. Flood, \"Fast splittable pseudorandom number generators\", OOPSLA 2014. The finalizer constants are those of SplitMix64."
msgstr "G. L. Steele、D. Lea 和 C. H. Flood，\"Fast splittable pseudorandom number generators\"，OOPSLA 2014。终结器常数取自 SplitMix64。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:47
msgid "Injectivity"
msgstr "单射性"

#: manual/design/generator.md:49
msgid "Each step is a bijection of 64-bit words:"
msgstr "每一步都是 64 位字上的双射："

#: manual/design/generator.md:51
msgid "$x \\mapsto x \\oplus a$ is its own inverse;"
msgstr "$x \\mapsto x \\oplus a$ 是它自身的逆；"

#: manual/design/generator.md:52
msgid "$x \\mapsto a\\,x$ with $a$ odd is invertible modulo $2^{64}$, because $\\gcd(a, 2^{64}) = 1$; all four multipliers (the FNV prime, the golden-ratio constant and the two finalizer constants) are odd;"
msgstr "当 $a$ 为奇数时，$x \\mapsto a\\,x$ 在模 $2^{64}$ 下可逆，因为 $\\gcd(a, 2^{64}) = 1$；全部四个乘数（FNV 素数、黄金比例常数和两个终结器常数）都是奇数；"

#: manual/design/generator.md:55
msgid "$x \\mapsto x \\oplus (x \\gg k)$ with $k \\ge 1$ is invertible: the top $k$ bits are unchanged, and each lower block of $k$ bits is recovered from the block above it."
msgstr "当 $k \\ge 1$ 时，$x \\mapsto x \\oplus (x \\gg k)$ 可逆：最高的 $k$ 位不变，较低的每个 $k$ 位块都可以由其上方的块恢复。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:59
msgid "Two consequences follow directly."
msgstr "由此直接得到两个推论。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:61
msgid "**Distinct indices never collide.** For fixed $s$ and $D$, $h_m$ is fixed, and $i \\mapsto z_0 \\mapsto z_1 \\mapsto z_2 \\mapsto$ result is a composition of bijections. Two datasets, repetitions or blocks with different ids get different seeds, for every run seed."
msgstr "**不同的索引永不碰撞。** 对固定的 $s$ 和 $D$，$h_m$ 是固定的，而 $i \\mapsto z_0 \\mapsto z_1 \\mapsto z_2 \\mapsto$ 结果是双射的复合。对于每个运行种子，id 不同的两个数据集、重复或区组都会得到不同的种子。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:65
msgid "**Distinct run seeds never collide.** For fixed $D$ and $i$, $s \\mapsto h_0$ is a bijection, every FNV step $h \\mapsto (h \\oplus c)\\,p$ is a bijection, and so is the rest. Changing the run seed changes every derived seed."
msgstr "**不同的运行种子永不碰撞。** 对固定的 $D$ 和 $i$，$s \\mapsto h_0$ 是双射，FNV 的每一步 $h \\mapsto (h \\oplus c)\\,p$ 都是双射，其余部分也是。改变运行种子会改变每个派生种子。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:69
msgid "For fixed $s$ and $i$, two domains collide exactly when their FNV states $h_m$ collide, because everything after $h_m$ is a bijection. Collisions are therefore possible only between different domains, or between different (domain, index) pairs with $h_m \\oplus i = h'_{m'} \\oplus i'$. Modelling FNV-1a as a random function, $N$ distinct domain strings collide with probability at most $\\binom N2 2^{-64} < N^2/2^{65}$; this is a heuristic, not a property of FNV-1a. The index enters through `Int::to_uint64`, which sign-extends and is injective, so negative indices are distinct from non-negative ones."
msgstr "对于固定的 $s$ 和 $i$，两个域恰好在它们的 FNV 状态 $h_m$ 碰撞时碰撞，因为 $h_m$ 之后的一切都是双射。因此碰撞只可能发生在不同的域之间，或者满足 $h_m \\oplus i = h'_{m'} \\oplus i'$ 的不同（域, 索引）对之间。把 FNV-1a 建模为随机函数时，$N$ 个不同的域字符串发生碰撞的概率至多为 $\\binom N2 2^{-64} < N^2/2^{65}$；这是一种启发式估计，而不是 FNV-1a 的性质。索引通过 `Int::to_uint64` 进入，它做符号扩展且是单射，因此负索引与非负索引互不相同。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:78
msgid "The finalizer gives avalanche: flipping one input bit flips each output bit with probability close to $1/2$. Consecutive indices therefore produce unrelated seeds even though $z_0$ differs between them only in low bits."
msgstr "终结器提供雪崩效应：翻转一个输入位会以接近 $1/2$ 的概率翻转每个输出位。因此，即使相邻索引的 $z_0$ 只在低位上不同，它们产生的种子也互不相关。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:82
msgid "Chained derivation"
msgstr "链式派生"

#: manual/design/generator.md:84
msgid "`measurement_seed(s, d, r, b)` applies `derive_seed` three times with the domains `\"dataset\"`, `\"repetition\"` and `\"block\"`. By consequence 2 applied to the outer calls and consequence 1 to each level, changing any one of $d$, $r$, $b$ with the others fixed changes the result."
msgstr "`measurement_seed(s, d, r, b)` 以域 `\"dataset\"`、`\"repetition\"` 和 `\"block\"` 三次应用 `derive_seed`。对外层调用应用推论 2，对每一层应用推论 1，可知在其他量固定时改变 $d$、$r$、$b$ 中的任何一个都会改变结果。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:91
msgid "`stable_fingerprint(x)` is `\"sha256:\"` followed by the hex digest of SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of $x$. Collisions require about $2^{128}$ work, so among $N$ fingerprints an accidental collision has probability at most $N^2/2^{257}$."
msgstr "`stable_fingerprint(x)` 为 `\"sha256:\"`，后接 $x$ 的 UTF-8 字节的 SHA-256 十六进制摘要。制造碰撞需要约 $2^{128}$ 的工作量，因此在 $N$ 个指纹中发生意外碰撞的概率至多为 $N^2/2^{257}$。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:98
msgid "Derived streams instead of one global generator"
msgstr "派生流，而非单一全局生成器"

#: manual/design/generator.md:100
msgid "*Problem.* With one random stream, adding a dataset or reordering calls changes every later input. *Choice.* Every consumer derives its own seed from the run seed, a domain and an index. *Why.* Inputs depend only on their names and ids, not on the order of generation, so a subset of datasets can be regenerated alone and adding a dataset does not change the others."
msgstr "*问题。* 如果只有一个随机流，增加一个数据集或调整调用顺序就会改变之后的每个输入。*选择。* 每个使用者都从运行种子、一个域和一个索引派生自己的种子。*理由。* 输入只取决于它们的名称和 id，而不取决于生成顺序，因此可以单独重新生成部分数据集，增加数据集也不会改变其他数据集。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:106
msgid "Integer mixing instead of a library generator"
msgstr "整数混合，而非库提供的生成器"

#: manual/design/generator.md:108
msgid "The derivation uses only multiplication, exclusive or and shifts on 64-bit integers, which every MoonBit backend implements identically. A float-based or platform generator could differ between native, JS and wasm."
msgstr "派生过程只使用 64 位整数上的乘法、异或和移位，每个 MoonBit 后端对它们的实现都完全相同。基于浮点或平台的生成器在 native、JS 和 wasm 之间可能不同。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:112
msgid "Code points, not bytes"
msgstr "码点，而非字节"

#: manual/design/generator.md:114
msgid "The domain is hashed one Unicode code point at a time. For ASCII domains this is standard FNV-1a; for other characters it differs from FNV-1a over UTF-8 bytes but is still deterministic. Use ASCII domain names if another tool must reproduce the seeds."
msgstr "域按 Unicode 码点逐个进行哈希。对 ASCII 域而言这就是标准的 FNV-1a；对其他字符，它与基于 UTF-8 字节的 FNV-1a 不同，但仍然是确定性的。如果其他工具必须复现这些种子，请使用 ASCII 域名称。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:119
msgid "SHA-256 fingerprints"
msgstr "SHA-256 指纹"

#: manual/design/generator.md:121
msgid "*Problem.* Inputs must be identified in artifacts without storing them. *Options.* FNV or another fast non-cryptographic hash; SHA-256. *Choice.* SHA-256 with an algorithm prefix. *Why.* Fingerprints are compared across machines and years; a collision would silently merge two inputs. The prefix leaves room for another algorithm without ambiguity."
msgstr "*问题。* 产物中必须能标识输入，而又不存储输入本身。*方案。* FNV 或其他快速的非密码学哈希；SHA-256。*选择。* 带算法前缀的 SHA-256。*理由。* 指纹要跨机器、跨年份进行比较；一次碰撞会悄无声息地把两个输入合并。前缀为将来使用其他算法留出了无歧义的余地。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:127
msgid "The runner passes the seed through"
msgstr "运行器原样传递种子"

#: manual/design/generator.md:129
msgid "The runner gives the fixture a `GenerationContext` with the run seed itself. The fixture decides which domains it needs and derives them, for example `derive_seed(context.seed, context.case_id, context.dataset_key.dataset_id)`. Keeping the derivation in the fixture lets one fixture draw several independent streams."
msgstr "运行器向夹具提供一个携带运行种子本身的 `GenerationContext`。由夹具决定它需要哪些域并自行派生，例如 `derive_seed(context.seed, context.case_id, context.dataset_key.dataset_id)`。把派生留在夹具中，使一个夹具可以抽取多个相互独立的流。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:137
msgid "**Determinism and portability.** Results depend only on the arguments and are bit-identical on every target."
msgstr "**确定性与可移植性。** 结果只取决于参数，并且在每个目标上逐位相同。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:139
msgid "**Injectivity** in the index and in the seed, as derived above."
msgstr "**单射性**：对索引和种子都成立，如上文所推导。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:140
msgid "**Fingerprint format.** Always `sha256:` followed by 64 lowercase hex digits."
msgstr "**指纹格式。** 总是 `sha256:` 后接 64 个小写十六进制数字。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:141
msgid "**Purity.** No function keeps state between calls."
msgstr "**纯粹性。** 没有函数在调用之间保留状态。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:145
msgid "**A stateful global random generator.** Order-dependent."
msgstr "**有状态的全局随机生成器。** 依赖顺序。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:146
msgid "**`seed + index`.** Adjacent seeds would feed correlated streams to generators that do not mix their seed."
msgstr "**`seed + index`。** 相邻的种子会把相关的流送给不混合其种子的生成器。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:148
msgid "**Content hashes with a fast non-cryptographic hash.** Too easy to collide for audit purposes."
msgstr "**用快速非密码学哈希计算内容哈希。** 对审计用途而言太容易碰撞。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:153
msgid "`generator` provides seeds, not random numbers: drawing values is the job of your generator function."
msgstr "`generator` 提供的是种子，而不是随机数：抽取值是你的生成器函数的工作。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:155
msgid "The derivation is not cryptographic: seeds can be predicted from the run seed, which is the point."
msgstr "派生过程不是密码学意义上的：种子可以从运行种子预测出来，这正是其目的所在。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:157
msgid "`stable_fingerprint` is unkeyed and does not authenticate data."
msgstr "`stable_fingerprint` 不带密钥，不能认证数据。"

#: manual/design/generator.md:158
msgid "Canonical serialization of inputs is up to the caller."
msgstr "输入的规范序列化由调用者负责。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:1
msgid "ir_model design"
msgstr "ir_model 设计"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:5
msgid "Separate what a report says from how it is drawn. Plot IR is a small, versioned data model that `report` produces from events and that any renderer (the built-in SVG/HTML, a notebook, a dashboard) can consume."
msgstr "把报告说了什么与它如何绘制分开。Plot IR 是一个小型的、带版本的数据模型，由 `report` 根据事件生成，任何渲染器（内置的 SVG/HTML、笔记本、仪表盘）都可以使用它。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:11
msgid "Scales are integers, shapes, layouts or names, so one axis type must cover them all."
msgstr "规模可以是整数、形状、布局或名称，因此一种坐标轴类型必须覆盖所有这些情况。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:13
msgid "Documents are read by renderers that may be newer or older than the writer."
msgstr "文档会被比写入者更新或更旧的渲染器读取。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:14
msgid "The IR carries data only; it computes nothing."
msgstr "IR 只承载数据；它不做任何计算。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:18
msgid "A plot is a finite multiset of points $(x, y, s)$ with a categorical $x$, a real $y$ and a series label $s$. The renderer's line through a series is the map"
msgstr "一张图表是点 $(x, y, s)$ 的有限多重集，其中 $x$ 是分类值，$y$ 是实数，$s$ 是系列标签。渲染器为某个系列绘制的线是映射"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:26
msgid "defined on the categories where the series has points. Because the points are kept, any other summary (median, quantiles) can be computed from the same IR without loss; a summary-only IR could not recover the points."
msgstr "定义在该系列有点的类别上。由于点被保留，任何其他摘要（中位数、分位数）都可以无损地从同一份 IR 计算出来；而只含摘要的 IR 无法恢复这些点。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:32
msgid "Categorical x"
msgstr "分类 x 轴"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:34
msgid "*Problem.* Scales are integers, shapes, layouts or names. *Choice.* `x` is a string. *Why.* One representation covers every scale type, and the order of first appearance is the order the producer chose. Numeric spacing would need a scale type in the IR."
msgstr "*问题。* 规模可能是整数、形状、布局或名称。*选择。* `x` 是字符串。*理由。* 一种表示即可覆盖每种规模类型，首次出现的顺序就是生成者选定的顺序。数值间距则需要在 IR 中引入规模类型。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:39
msgid "Raw points, not summaries"
msgstr "原始点，而非摘要"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:41
msgid "Points carry raw values; interval and summary plots are just plots whose points are summaries, labelled by `interval_kind`. The IR does not have to know which statistic produced a number."
msgstr "点携带原始值；区间图和摘要图只是其点为摘要的图表，由 `interval_kind` 标注。IR 不必知道是哪个统计量产生了某个数字。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:45
msgid "Differential evidence next to plots"
msgstr "差分证据与图表并列"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:47
msgid "The `DifferentialReport` lives in the same document as the plots. A renderer cannot show the timings of a run without having the correctness evidence of the same run at hand."
msgstr "`DifferentialReport` 与图表位于同一文档中。渲染器无法在手头没有同一次运行的正确性证据的情况下展示该运行的计时。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:51
msgid "A version in every document"
msgstr "每个文档都带版本"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:53
msgid "`schema_version` is set by `PlotDocument::new` to `mmks_2` and written into the JSON form, so consumers can reject documents they do not understand."
msgstr "`schema_version` 由 `PlotDocument::new` 设为 `mmks_2` 并写入 JSON 形式，供使用者拒绝无法识别的文档。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:58
msgid "`PlotDocument::new` always sets `schema_version` to `V2`; V1 is deprecated because it has no y-axis scale field."
msgstr "`PlotDocument::new` 始终将 `schema_version` 设为 `V2`；由于 V1 没有 y 轴刻度字段，V1 已弃用。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:60
msgid "`DifferentialReport::empty()` has no rows and zero counts."
msgstr "`DifferentialReport::empty()` 没有任何行，计数均为零。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:61
msgid "Records are plain data: no validation, no derived fields."
msgstr "记录是纯数据：没有验证，没有派生字段。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:65
msgid "**Renderer-inferred axes.** Rejected because a consumer must be able to reproduce the writer's coordinate mapping from the IR alone. Each plot carries both axis scales."
msgstr "**由渲染器推断刻度。** 不采用此方案，因为使用者必须能仅凭 IR 复现写入方的坐标映射。每个 plot 都携带两个轴的刻度类型。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:68
msgid "**A plotting library's specification format.** Would tie the IR to one renderer."
msgstr "**某个绘图库的规格格式。** 会把 IR 绑定到某一个渲染器。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:73
msgid "No rendering (that is `report`), no parsing, no statistics."
msgstr "没有渲染（那是 `report` 的工作）、没有解析、没有统计。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:74
msgid "The corpus total is not checked against the other counts."
msgstr "语料总数不会与其他计数进行核对。"

#: manual/design/ir_model.md:75
msgid "`PlotKind::Pareto` is a categorical scatter; there is no two-axis frontier in the IR."
msgstr "`PlotKind::Pareto` 是分类散点图；IR 中没有双坐标轴的前沿。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:1
msgid "ir_sink design"
msgstr "ir_sink 设计"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:5
msgid "Give applications one short import for the sinks that feed the report pipeline, without a second implementation of them."
msgstr "为应用提供一个简短的导入，用于获取向报告管线供数的接收器，而无需对它们进行第二次实现。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:10
msgid "It must not define behaviour of its own, so it cannot drift from `event`."
msgstr "它不得定义自己的行为，这样就不会与 `event` 产生偏离。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:11
msgid "Its values must mix freely with values built through `event`."
msgstr "它的值必须能与通过 `event` 构建的值自由混用。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:15
msgid "Each function of `ir_sink` equals an `event` function: `in_memory = InMemorySink::new`, `jsonl = JsonlSink::new`, `jsonl_stream = streaming_jsonl`, `tee = tee`. The package is the identity on behaviour; it only renames."
msgstr "`ir_sink` 的每个函数都等于一个 `event` 函数：`in_memory = InMemorySink::new`、`jsonl = JsonlSink::new`、`jsonl_stream = streaming_jsonl`、`tee = tee`。该包在行为上是恒等的；它只是重新命名。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:22
msgid "A facade, not a second sink layer"
msgstr "外观，而非第二层接收器"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:24
msgid "*Problem.* Examples and applications that only want \"events into JSONL for the report\" should not need to learn the full `event` surface. *Choice.* Four delegating functions. *Why.* Every behaviour is defined once, in `event`, so the facade cannot drift; the types it returns are the `event` types, so values from both packages mix freely."
msgstr "*问题。* 只想要“把事件写成 JSONL 供报告使用”的示例和应用，不应该需要学习 `event` 的全部接口。*选择。* 四个委托函数。*理由。* 每种行为只在 `event` 中定义一次，因此外观不会产生偏离；它返回的类型就是 `event` 的类型，因此两个包中的值可以自由混用。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:32
msgid "Every function returns exactly what the corresponding `event` function returns."
msgstr "每个函数返回的都恰好是相应 `event` 函数返回的内容。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:34
msgid "`ir_sink` depends only on `event`."
msgstr "`ir_sink` 只依赖 `event`。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:38
msgid "**Re-exporting with `pub using`.** Would also work; named functions keep the short names (`jsonl_stream`) independent of `event`'s names."
msgstr "**用 `pub using` 重新导出。** 也可行；具名函数使短名称（`jsonl_stream`）独立于 `event` 中的名称。"

#: manual/design/ir_sink.md:43
msgid "No sink types of its own, no file IO, no parsing."
msgstr "没有自己的接收器类型，没有文件 IO，没有解析。"

#: manual/design/model.md:1
msgid "model design"
msgstr "model 设计"

#: manual/design/model.md:5
msgid "Every other package exchanges data through `model`. The package fixes a vocabulary that is versioned, explicit about failure, and complete enough that a result can be traced back to its protocol, input and environment. It owns no behaviour beyond identities and accessors, so it can be depended on by every layer without cycles."
msgstr "其他每个包都通过 `model` 交换数据。该包确定了一套词汇：带版本、对失败显式表达，并且足够完整，使结果可以追溯到其协议、输入和环境。除身份函数和访问器外，它不拥有任何行为，因此每一层都可以依赖它而不会形成循环。"

#: manual/design/model.md:13
msgid "Every other package depends on `model`, directly or indirectly, so it can depend on nothing."
msgstr "其他每个包都直接或间接依赖 `model`，因此它不能依赖任何东西。"

#: manual/design/model.md:15
msgid "Records travel through JSONL artifacts that outlive the code that wrote them; their meaning must be pinned by a version."
msgstr "记录通过 JSONL 产物传递，而这些产物比写出它们的代码存活得更久；它们的含义必须由版本固定下来。"

#: manual/design/model.md:17
msgid "Values are read everywhere but should be built through one documented path."
msgstr "值在各处都会被读取，但应当通过一条有文档的路径来构建。"

#: manual/design/model.md:18
msgid "The package has no IO and no behaviour beyond identities and accessors."
msgstr "该包没有 IO，除了标识与访问器之外也没有任何行为。"

#: manual/design/model.md:22
msgid "Environment compatibility as an equivalence relation"
msgstr "作为等价关系的环境兼容性"

#: manual/design/model.md:24
msgid "Write an environment snapshot as $e = (\\sigma, \\pi, \\rho)$ with semantic part $\\sigma$, performance part $\\pi$ and provenance $\\rho$. `environment_compatible` is"
msgstr "把环境快照写作 $e = (\\sigma, \\pi, \\rho)$，其中 $\\sigma$ 为语义部分，$\\pi$ 为性能部分，$\\rho$ 为来源信息。`environment_compatible` 为"

#: manual/design/model.md:32
msgid "field by field. This is the kernel of the projection $p(e) = (\\sigma, \\pi)$: $e \\sim e' \\iff p(e) = p(e')$. The kernel of any map is an equivalence relation, since equality is reflexive, symmetric and transitive. Hence the snapshots of a set of runs split into classes, and comparisons are meaningful exactly within a class. Transitivity matters in practice: if run A may be compared with B and B with C, then A may be compared with C, so a baseline stored once can serve any later run of the same class."
msgstr "逐字段比较。这是投影 $p(e) = (\\sigma, \\pi)$ 的核：$e \\sim e' \\iff p(e) = p(e')$。任何映射的核都是等价关系，因为相等是自反、对称且传递的。因此，一组运行的快照会划分为若干类，比较恰好在同一类内才有意义。传递性在实践中很重要：如果运行 A 可以与 B 比较，B 可以与 C 比较，那么 A 就可以与 C 比较，因此一次存储的基线可以服务于同一类中之后的任何运行。"

#: manual/design/model.md:40
msgid "A relation with tolerances (for example \"CPU frequency within 5 %\") would not be transitive and would not split runs into classes; that is why the check is exact equality of declared strings."
msgstr "带容差的关系（例如“CPU 频率相差在 5 % 以内”）不是传递的，无法把运行划分为类；这就是检查采用声明字符串完全相等的原因。"

#: manual/design/model.md:44
msgid "Outcomes as a sum type"
msgstr "作为和类型的结果"

#: manual/design/model.md:46
msgid "An operation either produces a value or fails in one of several ways that deserve different treatment. Modelling the result as a sum,"
msgstr "一次操作要么产生一个值，要么以几种值得区别对待的方式之一失败。把结果建模为一个和类型，"

#: manual/design/model.md:53
msgid "keeps the cases apart in types, events and reports. `value_option` is the projection onto the first two summands; every other summand has no value, and a timed batch containing one is invalid."
msgstr "使各种情形在类型、事件和报告中保持区分。`value_option` 是到前两个分量上的投影；其他每个分量都没有值，包含它的计时批次是无效的。"

#: manual/design/model.md:59
msgid "Versioned identifiers"
msgstr "带版本的标识符"

#: manual/design/model.md:61
msgid "*Problem.* Readers of old JSONL must not silently misread new fields. *Choice.* Three version enums produce the identifiers `mmkp_1` (protocol vocabulary), `mmka_1` (event artifacts) and `mmks_2` (Plot IR). Every event carries `artifact_version`; readers reject unknown versions. *Why.* Additive changes keep the version; a breaking change adds `V2` and a lifecycle entry, and old readers fail loudly instead of guessing."
msgstr "`mmkp_1`（协议词汇）、`mmka_1`（事件产物）和 `mmks_2`（Plot IR）分别由三个版本枚举表示。每个事件都携带 `artifact_version`，读取器会拒绝未知版本。增量式更改沿用当前版本；破坏性更改会增加 `V2` 和生命周期条目，让旧读取器明确失败，而不是猜测新格式。"

#: manual/design/model.md:68
msgid "Three-part environment snapshots"
msgstr "三部分的环境快照"

#: manual/design/model.md:70
msgid "*Problem.* Some differences invalidate correctness (target, flags, ABI), some invalidate timings (CPU, GC, clock, frequency policy), and some are just bookkeeping (hostname, time, revision). *Choice.* `SemanticEnvironment`, `PerformanceEnvironment` and `ProvenanceEnvironment`, with compatibility on the first two. *Why.* Two runs on different hosts with the same declared hardware remain comparable; a run with different flags does not. The snapshot records what you declare; mare_mark does not probe the machine."
msgstr "*问题。* 有些差异会使正确性失效（目标、标志、ABI），有些会使计时失效（CPU、GC、时钟、频率策略），还有些只是簿记信息（主机名、时间、修订版本）。*选择。* `SemanticEnvironment`、`PerformanceEnvironment` 和 `ProvenanceEnvironment`，兼容性取决于前两者。*理由。* 在不同主机上、声明的硬件相同的两次运行仍然可以比较；标志不同的运行则不行。快照记录的是你声明的内容；mare_mark 不会探测机器。"

#: manual/design/model.md:78
msgid "Explicit protocols"
msgstr "显式的协议"

#: manual/design/model.md:80
msgid "*Problem.* \"Ran the benchmark\" hides warmup, batch sizes, order, sample counts and the decision threshold. *Choice.* `RunProtocol` names all of them, and `protocol_identity` folds the warmup count, the confirmatory sample count and the practical threshold into a short key. *Why.* A result is reproducible only if its protocol is. The key is deliberately short and does not cover every field; store the full protocol next to results that will be compared."
msgstr "*问题。* “跑了基准测试”掩盖了预热、批次大小、顺序、样本数和决策阈值。*选择。* `RunProtocol` 为所有这些命名，`protocol_identity` 把预热次数、验证性样本数和实际阈值折叠成一个短键。*理由。* 只有协议可复现，结果才可复现。该键有意保持简短，并不覆盖每个字段；请在将要比较的结果旁存储完整的协议。"

#: manual/design/model.md:87
msgid "Failure kinds instead of strings"
msgstr "失败种类，而非字符串"

#: manual/design/model.md:89
msgid "`ExecutionOutcome` distinguishes a worker crash (`Aborted`) from a timeout, a decoding problem, an unsupported input and an accepted deviation, and `ValidationStatus` mirrors that on the oracle side. Reports count each kind in the capability matrix, so \"unsupported\" never reads as \"wrong\" and a timeout never reads as a slow measurement."
msgstr "`ExecutionOutcome` 把工作进程崩溃（`Aborted`）与超时、解码问题、不受支持的输入和被接受的偏差区分开来，`ValidationStatus` 在判定器一侧与之对应。报告在能力矩阵中分别统计每一种，因此“不支持”永远不会被读成“错误”，超时也永远不会被读成一次慢的测量。"

#: manual/design/model.md:95
msgid "Read-only records with constructors"
msgstr "带构造函数的只读记录"

#: manual/design/model.md:97
msgid "Records are `pub struct`: fields are readable everywhere, values are built through `new`. Enums that users need to build are `pub(all)`. `IntervalMode` and `CrossoverResult` are built through functions so that their construction stays a single, documented path."
msgstr "记录是 `pub struct`：字段在任何地方都可读，值通过 `new` 构建。用户需要构建的枚举是 `pub(all)`。`IntervalMode` 和 `CrossoverResult` 通过函数构建，使其构造始终只有一条有文档记录的路径。"

#: manual/design/model.md:102
msgid "Decision and deployment types"
msgstr "决策与部署类型"

#: manual/design/model.md:104
msgid "`ScaleBoundary`, `Region`, `ParetoPoint`, `DeploymentPolicy` and `CrossoverResult` describe how a measured preference becomes a deployment rule. They live in `model` so that `experiment`, `tune` and applications agree on them without depending on each other."
msgstr "`ScaleBoundary`、`Region`、`ParetoPoint`、`DeploymentPolicy` 和 `CrossoverResult` 描述测得的偏好如何成为部署规则。它们位于 `model` 中，使 `experiment`、`tune` 和应用无需相互依赖即可对它们达成一致。"

#: manual/design/model.md:111
msgid "`environment_compatible` is an equivalence relation (derived above)."
msgstr "`environment_compatible` 是一个等价关系（推导见上文）。"

#: manual/design/model.md:112
msgid "`X::identifier()` is `implementation() + \"_\" + version()` for every version enum, and the `V1` values are `Supported`."
msgstr "对每个版本枚举，`X::identifier()` 都是 `implementation() + \"_\" + version()`，且 `V1` 值都是 `Supported`。"

#: manual/design/model.md:114
msgid "`ExecutionOutcome::value_option(o)` is `Some` exactly for `Value` and `RaisedFlags`; `flags(o)` is non-empty only for `RaisedFlags` and `Trapped`."
msgstr "`ExecutionOutcome::value_option(o)` 恰好对 `Value` 和 `RaisedFlags` 为 `Some`；`flags(o)` 只对 `RaisedFlags` 和 `Trapped` 非空。"

#: manual/design/model.md:116
msgid "`OperationResult::completed(v, c)` equals `OperationResult::new(Value(v), Some(c))` with empty output and no exit code."
msgstr "`OperationResult::completed(v, c)` 等于输出为空且没有退出码的 `OperationResult::new(Value(v), Some(c))`。"

#: manual/design/model.md:118
msgid "Constructors copy nothing and validate nothing: validation belongs to `runner.validate_protocol` and `BenchSpec::compile`."
msgstr "构造函数不复制任何东西，也不验证任何东西：验证属于 `runner.validate_protocol` 和 `BenchSpec::compile`。"

#: manual/design/model.md:123
msgid "**Probing the environment.** Reading CPU model, governor and GC settings needs per-platform code and permissions; declared values are explicit and testable."
msgstr "**探测环境。** 读取 CPU 型号、调速器和 GC 设置需要针对各平台的代码和权限；声明的值则是显式且可测试的。"

#: manual/design/model.md:126
msgid "**Tolerant compatibility.** Not transitive (see above)."
msgstr "**带容差的兼容性。** 不具有传递性（见上文）。"

#: manual/design/model.md:127
msgid "**Free-form outcome strings.** Lose the distinction between failure kinds."
msgstr "**自由格式的结果字符串。** 会丢失失败种类之间的区分。"

#: manual/design/model.md:128
msgid "**One flat protocol string.** Unreadable and unvalidated."
msgstr "**单个扁平的协议字符串。** 不可读且未经验证。"

#: manual/design/model.md:132
msgid "No validation of values; no IO; no serialization (JSON lives in `event`, `report` and `tune_gemm`)."
msgstr "不验证值；没有 IO；没有序列化（JSON 位于 `event`、`report` 和 `tune_gemm` 中）。"

#: manual/design/model.md:134
msgid "`protocol_identity` covers three fields only."
msgstr "`protocol_identity` 只覆盖三个字段。"

#: manual/design/model.md:135
msgid "`ExperimentDesign`, `ValidationCoverage`, `OutlierPolicy` and `WorkspaceScope` are recorded intent; the runner does not interpret them."
msgstr "`ExperimentDesign`、`ValidationCoverage`、`OutlierPolicy` 和 `WorkspaceScope` 是记录下来的意图；运行器不解释它们。"

#: manual/design/model.md:137
msgid "`ProtocolVersion`, `ArtifactVersion` and `SchemaVersion` have one version each; there is no migration code."
msgstr "`ProtocolVersion`、`ArtifactVersion` 和 `SchemaVersion` 各只有一个版本；没有迁移代码。"

#: manual/design/report.md:1
msgid "report design"
msgstr "report 设计"

#: manual/design/report.md:5
msgid "A benchmark report must be reproducible from the audit record and safe to share. `report` is a pure projection from the JSONL event stream to Plot IR (`ir_model`) and from Plot IR to JSON, SVG and HTML. It never decides what is fast; it shows what the stream contains, and it never lets an invalid measurement look like a valid one."
msgstr "基准测试报告必须能从审计记录复现，并且可以安全地分享。`report` 是一个纯投影：从 JSONL 事件流到 Plot IR（`ir_model`），再从 Plot IR 到 JSON、SVG 和 HTML。它从不判定什么更快；它展示流中包含的内容，并且绝不让一次无效的测量看起来像有效的。"

#: manual/design/report.md:13
msgid "The same JSONL must give the same bytes on every target, so the functions are pure and do no IO."
msgstr "相同的 JSONL 必须在每个目标上给出相同的字节，因此这些函数是纯的，不做 IO。"

#: manual/design/report.md:15
msgid "The HTML must render without network access, years later."
msgstr "HTML 必须在没有网络访问的情况下渲染，即使多年以后。"

#: manual/design/report.md:16
msgid "Strings in events come from payloads and may contain markup."
msgstr "事件中的字符串来自负载，可能包含标记。"

#: manual/design/report.md:20
msgid "The projection"
msgstr "投影"

#: manual/design/report.md:22
msgid "Let the stream be a sequence of events. Write $O$ for the observations with `valid` true and `batch_sink` `\"kept\"`, and $F$ for the set of keys $(\\text{case}, \\text{implementation}, \\text{dataset})$ of validations whose status is `invalid` or `infrastructure_failure`. The plotted points are"
msgstr "设流是一个事件序列。用 $O$ 表示 `valid` 为真且 `batch_sink` 为 `\"kept\"` 的观测，用 $F$ 表示状态为 `invalid` 或 `infrastructure_failure` 的验证所对应的键 $(\\text{case}, \\text{implementation}, \\text{dataset})$ 的集合。绘制的点为"

#: manual/design/report.md:31
msgid "in stream order. The projection is monotone in the evidence against a point: adding a failing validation can only remove points, adding an invalid observation adds none."
msgstr "按流中的顺序排列。该投影对于不利于某个点的证据是单调的：增加一个失败的验证只会移除点，增加一个无效观测不会添加任何点。"

#: manual/design/report.md:35
msgid "Coordinates"
msgstr "坐标"

#: manual/design/report.md:37
msgid "A plot occupies the rectangle $[76, 880] \\times [102, 354]$ of a $960 \\times 420$ view box. With $m$ distinct x categories in order of first appearance, category $i$ is placed at"
msgstr "一张图表占据 $960 \\times 420$ 视框中的矩形 $[76, 880] \\times [102, 354]$。若按首次出现顺序有 $m$ 个不同的 x 类别，则类别 $i$ 位于"

#: manual/design/report.md:45
msgid "Let $v_{\\min}$ and $v_{\\max}$ be the extreme y values. The y range is padded,"
msgstr "设 $v_{\\min}$ 和 $v_{\\max}$ 为 y 的极值。y 的范围会加上留白，"

#: manual/design/report.md:55
msgid "and $[0, 1]$ for an empty plot. For finite values and in exact arithmetic, $h - \\ell > 0$ in every case, so the linear map"
msgstr "空图表则为 $[0, 1]$。对于有限值并在精确算术下，每种情况都有 $h - \\ell > 0$，因此线性映射"

#: manual/design/report.md:62
msgid "is well defined, and for every plotted value $\\ell < v < h$, which places every point strictly inside the plot area. In floating point the padding can be lost to rounding when $w$ is tiny compared with $\\lvert v\\rvert$, and an infinite or `NaN` value breaks the bounds; the renderer does not filter them. Heatmap cells use the opacity $0.18 + 0.72\\,(v - \\ell)/(h - \\ell)$, which therefore lies strictly between $0.18$ and $0.90$: no cell is invisible and none is fully saturated."
msgstr "是良定义的，并且对每个绘制的值都有 $\\ell < v < h$，这使每个点都严格位于绘图区域内部。在浮点运算中，当 $w$ 相对于 $\\lvert v\\rvert$ 极小时，填充可能因舍入而丢失；无穷大或 `NaN` 的值会破坏这些边界，而渲染器不会过滤它们。热力图单元格使用不透明度 $0.18 + 0.72\\,(v - \\ell)/(h - \\ell)$，因此它严格介于 $0.18$ 和 $0.90$ 之间：没有单元格是不可见的，也没有单元格是完全饱和的。"

#: manual/design/report.md:69
msgid "Grid lines are drawn at $Y = 102 + 63j$ for $j = 0, \\dots, 4$ with tick value $h - (h - \\ell)\\,j/4$, rounded to three decimals; magnitudes below $0.001$ or from $10^{15}$ up keep their shortest round-trip form, because rounding would erase or overflow them. With $m$ categories, labels are drawn every $\\lceil m/10\\rceil$ categories and at the last one, so at most eleven labels are shown."
msgstr "网格线绘制在 $Y = 102 + 63j$ 处（$j = 0, \\dots, 4$），刻度值为 $h - (h - \\ell)\\,j/4$，四舍五入到三位小数；绝对值小于 $0.001$ 或不小于 $10^{15}$ 的数保留最短往返表示，因为舍入会抹去或溢出这些值。若有 $m$ 个类别，则每隔 $\\lceil m/10\\rceil$ 个类别以及在最后一个类别处绘制标签，因此最多显示十一个标签。"

#: manual/design/report.md:78
msgid "A pure projection with the effects outside"
msgstr "纯投影，副作用在外"

#: manual/design/report.md:80
msgid "*Problem.* Reports are regenerated after renderer changes and compared in review. *Choice.* `document_from_jsonl`, `plot_json`, `plot_svg` and `html` take values and return strings; file IO, standard streams and opening a browser live in the [`cli`](cli.md). *Why.* The same JSONL gives the same bytes on every target, tests need no filesystem, and the HTML can be produced inside a larger application."
msgstr "*问题。* 渲染器改动后需要重新生成报告，并在评审中进行比较。*选择。* `document_from_jsonl`、`plot_json`、`plot_svg` 和 `html` 接收值并返回字符串；文件 IO、标准流和打开浏览器都位于 [`cli`](cli.md) 中。*理由。* 同一份 JSONL 在每个目标上都给出相同的字节，测试不需要文件系统，HTML 也可以在更大的应用中生成。"

#: manual/design/report.md:87
msgid "Failures remove series and stay visible"
msgstr "失败会移除系列，并保持可见"

#: manual/design/report.md:89
msgid "*Problem.* A fast implementation that returns wrong results would look like a win. *Choice.* A failing validation removes the points of that implementation for that case and dataset, and adds a mismatch row; minimized failures add a counterexample row with the replay command. *Why.* The differential section sits above the plots, so the reader sees why a series is missing."
msgstr "*问题。* 一个返回错误结果的快速实现看起来会像是赢家。*选择。* 失败的验证会移除该实现在该用例和数据集上的点，并添加一行不匹配记录；最小化后的失败会添加一行带重放命令的反例。*理由。* 差分部分位于图表上方，因此读者能看到某个系列缺失的原因。"

#: manual/design/report.md:95
msgid "Raw points with mean lines"
msgstr "原始点加均值线"

#: manual/design/report.md:97
msgid "*Problem.* Summaries hide distributions, raw clouds hide trends. *Choice.* Every observation is drawn with a tooltip, and for line kinds the per-category mean connects the categories. *Why.* The mean of the drawn points is the centre of mass the eye already estimates; robust statistics and decisions belong to `stats` and can be added as further plots. The line is a guide, not an estimate the report vouches for."
msgstr "*问题。* 摘要掩盖分布，原始点云掩盖趋势。*选择。* 每个观测都带提示地绘制出来，对于线型图表，各类别的均值把类别连接起来。*理由。* 所绘各点的均值正是肉眼已经在估计的重心；稳健统计和决策属于 `stats`，可以作为更多图表添加。这条线是参考线，而不是报告为之担保的估计。"

#: manual/design/report.md:104
msgid "Axis selection for scaling plots"
msgstr "## 缩放图的轴选择"

#: manual/design/report.md:106
msgid "`PlotPoint.x` remains text so a scale can be an integer, shape, layout or name. For scaling plots, finite numeric x values are ordered numerically and placed on a linear axis unless all are positive and `max / min >= 100`; then x uses `log10(x)`. Y is evaluated independently by the same rule. This span is at least two decades and gives multiplicative changes equal distances because log10(b) - log10(a) = log10(b / a). If any value on an axis is non-finite or non-positive, or if the positive finite values span less than 100×, that axis stays linear. A nonnumeric x axis stays categorical in first-appearance order. Heatmaps also keep categorical x."
msgstr "`PlotPoint.x` 仍以文本表示，以便刻度可以是整数、形状、布局或名称。对缩放图而言，有限数值 x 按数值排序；除非所有值均为正且 `max / min >= 100`，此时 x 轴才使用 `log10(x)`。y 轴按相同规则独立判断。该跨度至少为两个数量级，能让相同倍数的变化占据相同距离，因为 log10(b) - log10(a) = log10(b / a)。如果轴上的任一值不是有限正数，或正有限值的跨度小于 100 倍，该轴保持线性。非数值 x 轴仍按首次出现顺序作为分类轴。热图的 x 轴也保持分类刻度。"

#: manual/design/report.md:116
msgid "Log-axis ticks lie within the observed data range, and labels stay at least 56 px apart on x and 28 px apart on y. Every power of ten in range is labelled; when decades are closer than that spacing, only the powers whose exponent is divisible by the smallest k that keeps them apart are labelled, so the labels stay uniform. The `2 × 10^k` and `5 × 10^k` ticks are added only when a decade is wide enough to keep every label that far apart. A range that holds no `1, 2, 5 × 10^k` value labels its endpoints, and a single value is labelled at the centre of the axis. Grid lines are drawn only at labelled ticks, so their number stays bounded however many decades the data span. Tick labels use the same number format as linear axes. The SVG records each chosen axis scale in Plot IR and JSON, and the plot note and axis label identify any log transform."
msgstr "对数轴刻度位于观测数据范围内，标签间距在 x 轴上至少为 56 px，在 y 轴上至少为 28 px。范围内的每个十的幂都会标注；当十进位间距小于该间距时，只标注指数能被最小的、足以保持间距的 k 整除的幂，使标签保持均匀。只有当一个十进位足够宽、能使所有标签保持该间距时，才添加 `2 × 10^k` 和 `5 × 10^k` 刻度。若范围内没有任何 `1, 2, 5 × 10^k` 值，则标注两个端点；单个值标注在轴的中央。网格线只绘制在已标注的刻度处，因此无论数据跨越多少个十进位，其数量都有上界。刻度标签与线性轴使用相同的数字格式。SVG 在 Plot IR 和 JSON 中记录每个选定的轴刻度，图表注释和轴标签会标明对数变换。"

#: manual/design/report.md:128
msgid "Escaping order"
msgstr "转义顺序"

#: manual/design/report.md:130
msgid "Text is escaped by replacing `&`, `<`, `>`, `\"` and `'` in this order. `&` must be first: replacing it after `<` would turn the produced `&lt;` into `&amp;lt;`. Since every later replacement introduces only `&` that is already part of an entity, the result decodes back to the input exactly once. The same function escapes element text and attribute values."
msgstr "文本转义按此顺序替换 `&`、`<`、`>`、`\"` 和 `'`。`&` 必须排在最前：若在 `<` 之后再替换它，生成的 `&lt;` 就会变成 `&amp;lt;`。由于之后的每次替换引入的 `&` 都已经是某个实体的一部分，结果恰好能解码回输入一次。同一个函数既转义元素文本，也转义属性值。"

#: manual/design/report.md:136
msgid "Self-contained output"
msgstr "自包含的输出"

#: manual/design/report.md:138
msgid "The HTML embeds its CSS and inline SVG, loads no fonts, scripts or images, and declares `color-scheme: light`. It can be attached to an issue or archived with the JSONL and still render identically in ten years."
msgstr "HTML 内嵌其 CSS 和内联 SVG，不加载任何字体、脚本或图像，并声明 `color-scheme: light`。它可以作为附件添加到 issue 中，或与 JSONL 一起归档，十年后渲染效果依然相同。"

#: manual/design/report.md:142
msgid "Version gate"
msgstr "版本关卡"

#: manual/design/report.md:144
msgid "A line whose `artifact_version` is a string other than `mmka_1` is rejected with its line number. Lines without the field are accepted, so hand-written fixtures and earlier streams stay readable; a non-string version is an error. JSON output carries `schema_version` `mmks_2` and each plot's x and y axis scales. This version change lets consumers distinguish documents whose y-axis mapping is explicit from older `mmks_1` documents."
msgstr "JSON 输出使用 `schema_version` `mmks_2`，每个 plot 都记录 x、y 轴刻度。版本升级让读取器能区分轴映射明确的新文档与旧版 `mmks_1` 文档。"

#: manual/design/report.md:153
msgid "**Determinism.** Every function is pure; equal inputs give equal strings."
msgstr "**确定性。** 每个函数都是纯函数；相等的输入给出相等的字符串。"

#: manual/design/report.md:154
msgid "**Exclusion.** No point comes from an observation that is invalid, discarded or covered by a failing validation (definition of $P$)."
msgstr "**排除。** 没有点来自无效的、被丢弃的或被失败验证覆盖的观测（$P$ 的定义）。"

#: manual/design/report.md:156
msgid "**Containment.** For finite values, every point lies strictly inside the plot area, and every heatmap opacity lies in $(0.18, 0.90)$ (derived above)."
msgstr "**包含。** 对于有限值，每个点都严格位于绘图区域内部，每个热力图不透明度都位于 $(0.18, 0.90)$ 中（推导见上文）。"

#: manual/design/report.md:158
msgid "**Escaping.** All text originating from events, titles, units and series names passes through the escape function before reaching SVG or HTML."
msgstr "**转义。** 所有来自事件、标题、单位和系列名称的文本在进入 SVG 或 HTML 之前都会经过转义函数。"

#: manual/design/report.md:160
msgid "**Complexity.** Parsing is linear in the stream size, except that each point is checked against the list of failure keys, $O(\\lvert O\\rvert \\cdot \\lvert F\\rvert)$. Rendering a plot with $N$ points, $m$ categories and $S$ series is $O(N(m + S) + mSN)$ because line means are recomputed per cell."
msgstr "**复杂度。** 解析与流的大小成线性关系，只是每个点都要与失败键列表比对，代价为 $O(\\lvert O\\rvert \\cdot \\lvert F\\rvert)$。渲染含 $N$ 个点、$m$ 个类别和 $S$ 个系列的图表需要 $O(N(m + S) + mSN)$，因为每个单元格都会重新计算线的均值。"

#: manual/design/report.md:167
msgid "**A JavaScript charting library.** It would need scripts or a CDN and would make the output depend on a browser runtime."
msgstr "**JavaScript 图表库。** 它需要脚本或 CDN，并会使输出依赖浏览器运行时。"

#: manual/design/report.md:169
msgid "**Rendering only summaries.** Hides bimodality and outliers."
msgstr "**只渲染摘要。** 会掩盖双峰性和离群值。"

#: manual/design/report.md:170
msgid "**One axis policy for both dimensions.** Rejected because x and y can have different ranges and need independent scale choices."
msgstr "**两维共用一种轴策略。** 不采用此方案，因为 x 和 y 的取值范围可能不同，必须分别选择刻度。"

#: manual/design/report.md:172
msgid "**Treating failed implementations as zero or infinite time.** Both are misleading values on a timing axis."
msgstr "**把失败的实现视为零时间或无穷时间。** 在计时坐标轴上，两者都是误导性的值。"

#: manual/design/report.md:177
msgid "The JSONL projection builds one `Scaling` plot. Other plot kinds are rendered when a caller constructs them in Plot IR, but nothing derives them from events yet."
msgstr "JSONL 投影只构建一张 `Scaling` 图表。当调用者在 Plot IR 中构造其他种类的图表时它们也会被渲染，但目前还没有任何代码从事件中派生它们。"

#: manual/design/report.md:180
msgid "Observations of exploratory and confirmatory phases are plotted together, and the x value is the dataset index, not the scale."
msgstr "探索性阶段和验证性阶段的观测绘制在一起，x 值是数据集索引，而不是规模。"

#: manual/design/report.md:182
msgid "The target is passed in by the caller; it is not read from the stream."
msgstr "目标由调用者传入；它不是从流中读取的。"

#: manual/design/report.md:183
msgid "No statistics, decisions or environment comparison are computed here."
msgstr "这里不计算统计量、决策或环境比较。"

#: manual/design/report.md:184
msgid "Styling, colours and layout are not a compatibility promise; the `mmks_2` JSON structure is."
msgstr "样式、颜色和布局不属于兼容性承诺；`mmks_2` JSON 结构才是。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:1
msgid "runner design"
msgstr "runner 设计"

#: manual/design/runner.md:5
msgid "A benchmark result is evidence only if three things hold: the implementations computed the right answer on the measured input, every implementation was measured under the same conditions, and the measurement can be traced back to a seed, a protocol and an environment. `runner` is the one package that executes payloads, and it is built so that these properties hold by construction rather than by discipline: validation precedes timing, the order of implementations is balanced, batch sizes are calibrated, and every raw observation is emitted."
msgstr "基准测试结果只有在三件事都成立时才能作为证据：各实现在被测量的输入上算出了正确答案，每个实现都在相同条件下被测量，并且测量可以追溯到一个种子、一个协议和一个环境。`runner` 是唯一执行负载的包，它的构建方式使这些性质依靠构造而非依靠自律成立：验证先于计时，实现的顺序是平衡的，批次大小经过校准，每个原始观测都会被发出。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:15
msgid "It is the only package that executes payloads, and payloads may be wrong, slow, crash or loop."
msgstr "它是唯一执行负载的包，而负载可能出错、缓慢、崩溃或死循环。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:17
msgid "Timers have a finite resolution (`performance.now()` may be coarsened to 100 µs or more in browsers), and machines drift during a run."
msgstr "计时器的分辨率有限（浏览器中的 `performance.now()` 可能被降低到 100 µs 或更粗），而且机器在运行期间会漂移。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:19
msgid "`run` is asynchronous and must work wherever `moonbitlang/async` has a runtime; subprocesses exist only on native."
msgstr "`run` 是异步的，必须在 `moonbitlang/async` 提供运行时的任何地方工作；子进程只存在于 native 上。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:21
msgid "No event may be emitted inside a timed region."
msgstr "计时区域内不得发出任何事件。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:25
msgid "Blocks and the measurement model"
msgstr "区组与测量模型"

#: manual/design/runner.md:27
msgid "For one dataset the runner measures $k$ implementations in blocks $b = 0, 1, \\dots, E + C - 1$: $E$ exploratory blocks followed by $C$ confirmatory blocks (`exploratory_samples` and `confirmatory_samples`). Inside a block every implementation runs one batch. Model the per-iteration time of implementation $i$ in block $b$ as"
msgstr "对于一个数据集，运行器在区组 $b = 0, 1, \\dots, E + C - 1$ 中测量 $k$ 个实现：先是 $E$ 个探索性区组，然后是 $C$ 个验证性区组（`exploratory_samples` 和 `confirmatory_samples`）。在一个区组内，每个实现运行一个批次。把实现 $i$ 在区组 $b$ 中的每次迭代时间建模为"

#: manual/design/runner.md:37
msgid "where $p_i(b) \\in \\{0, \\dots, k-1\\}$ is the position of $i$ inside the block, $\\tau_p$ a position effect (the first batch of a block runs with colder caches), $s_i(b) = bk + p_i(b)$ the global slot number, $\\delta$ a linear drift (thermal throttling, background load) and $\\varepsilon$ noise. The quantity of interest is $\\mu_j - \\mu_i$."
msgstr "其中 $p_i(b) \\in \\{0, \\dots, k-1\\}$ 是 $i$ 在区组内的位置，$\\tau_p$ 是位置效应（区组的第一个批次在较冷的缓存下运行），$s_i(b) = bk + p_i(b)$ 是全局槽位编号，$\\delta$ 是线性漂移（热降频、后台负载），$\\varepsilon$ 是噪声。我们关心的量是 $\\mu_j - \\mu_i$。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:43
msgid "Cyclic Latin square order"
msgstr "循环拉丁方顺序"

#: manual/design/runner.md:45
msgid "Under `OrderPolicy::BalancedBlocks(order_seed)` block $b$ runs the implementations in the order `balanced_order(k, b + o)`, that is implementation $(p + b + o) \\bmod k$ at position $p$, with offset $o = (\\text{order\\_seed} \\oplus \\text{run\\_seed}) \\bmod k$. Implementation $i$ therefore sits at position"
msgstr "在 `OrderPolicy::BalancedBlocks(order_seed)` 下，区组 $b$ 按 `balanced_order(k, b + o)` 的顺序运行各实现，即位置 $p$ 上是实现 $(p + b + o) \\bmod k$，偏移量为 $o = (\\text{order\\_seed} \\oplus \\text{run\\_seed}) \\bmod k$。因此实现 $i$ 位于位置"

#: manual/design/runner.md:55
msgid "**Balance.** For fixed $i$, the map $b \\mapsto (i - b - o) \\bmod k$ is a bijection from any $k$ consecutive integers onto $\\{0, \\dots, k-1\\}$. Over every complete cycle of $k$ consecutive blocks each implementation occupies each position exactly once: the $k \\times k$ table of positions is a Latin square."
msgstr "**平衡性。** 对固定的 $i$，映射 $b \\mapsto (i - b - o) \\bmod k$ 是从任意 $k$ 个连续整数到 $\\{0, \\dots, k-1\\}$ 的双射。在由 $k$ 个连续区组构成的每个完整周期中，每个实现恰好在每个位置出现一次：$k \\times k$ 的位置表是一个拉丁方。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:60
msgid "**Cancellation.** Sum the model over a complete cycle $b_0, \\dots, b_0 + k - 1$:"
msgstr "**抵消。** 在一个完整周期 $b_0, \\dots, b_0 + k - 1$ 上对模型求和："

#: manual/design/runner.md:69
msgid "Both right-hand sides are independent of $i$. The cycle means therefore satisfy"
msgstr "两个等式的右侧都与 $i$ 无关。因此周期均值满足"

#: manual/design/runner.md:75
msgid "free of position effects and of linear drift. With `FixedOrder`, $p_i(b) = i$ in every block and the difference carries the bias $\\tau_j - \\tau_i + \\delta (j - i)$ for ever."
msgstr "不受位置效应和线性漂移影响。使用 `FixedOrder` 时，每个区组中都有 $p_i(b) = i$，差值将永远带有偏差 $\\tau_j - \\tau_i + \\delta (j - i)$。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:79
msgid "The cancellation is exact for means over complete cycles; choose $E + C$ as a multiple of $k$ so that the confirmatory phase, which continues the rotation at block $E$, covers complete cycles. Medians of paired deltas are robust rather than exactly unbiased: the per-block bias $\\tau_{p_j(b)} - \\tau_{p_i(b)} + \\delta (p_j(b) - p_i(b))$ takes each of its $k$ values equally often, and for $k = 2$ it alternates between $+c$ and $-c$."
msgstr "对完整周期上的均值而言，抵消是精确的；请把 $E + C$ 选为 $k$ 的倍数，使从区组 $E$ 开始继续轮换的验证性阶段覆盖完整的周期。成对差值的中位数是稳健的，而不是精确无偏的：每个区组的偏差 $\\tau_{p_j(b)} - \\tau_{p_i(b)} + \\delta (p_j(b) - p_i(b))$ 以相同的频率取其 $k$ 个值中的每一个，当 $k = 2$ 时它在 $+c$ 和 $-c$ 之间交替。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:86
msgid "Batch calibration"
msgstr "批次校准"

#: manual/design/runner.md:88
msgid "A timer has a resolution $\\rho$ and a start/stop overhead $\\omega$. A batch of $n$ iterations that truly takes $T(n)$ is read as $\\hat T = T(n) + \\omega + q$ with $\\lvert q\\rvert \\le \\rho$, and the runner reports $\\hat T / n$. The relative error of the per-iteration time is at most"
msgstr "计时器具有分辨率 $\\rho$ 和启动/停止开销 $\\omega$。一个实际耗时 $T(n)$ 的 $n$ 次迭代批次被读作 $\\hat T = T(n) + \\omega + q$，其中 $\\lvert q\\rvert \\le \\rho$，运行器报告 $\\hat T / n$。每次迭代时间的相对误差至多为"

#: manual/design/runner.md:97
msgid "which shrinks as the batch grows. Calibration chooses $n$ so that $T(n)$ reaches `target_batch_time_us` $= t$. Starting from $n_0 = \\min(\\max(\\text{min\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1), n_{\\max})$ with $n_{\\max} = \\max(\\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1)$, while the batch is valid, $T(n) < t$, $T(n) <$ `max_sample_time_us` and $n <$ `max_batch_iterations`, the next size is"
msgstr "它随批次增大而减小。校准选择 $n$，使 $T(n)$ 达到 `target_batch_time_us` $= t$。从 $n_0 = \\min(\\max(\\text{min\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1), n_{\\max})$（其中 $n_{\\max} = \\max(\\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1)$）开始，只要批次有效、$T(n) < t$、$T(n) <$ `max_sample_time_us` 且 $n <$ `max_batch_iterations`，下一个批次大小为"

#: manual/design/runner.md:108
msgid "with $10\\, n_j$ in place of the ratio when the measured time is $0$."
msgstr "当测得的时间为 $0$ 时，用 $10\\, n_j$ 代替该比值。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:110
msgid "*Linear cost.* If $T(n) = c\\,n$, the first update gives $n_1 = \\lceil t / c\\rceil$ and $T(n_1) \\in [t, t + c)$: one retry suffices."
msgstr "*线性代价。* 若 $T(n) = c\\,n$，第一次更新给出 $n_1 = \\lceil t / c\\rceil$ 且 $T(n_1) \\in [t, t + c)$：一次重试就足够。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:113
msgid "*Affine cost.* If $T(n) = a + c\\,n$ with a fixed per-batch cost $a > 0$, the update is the fixed-point iteration of $f(n) = n t / (a + c n)$. Its fixed point solves $a + c n^* = t$, so $n^* = (t - a)/c$, and"
msgstr "*仿射代价。* 若 $T(n) = a + c\\,n$，其中每批次固定代价 $a > 0$，则更新就是 $f(n) = n t / (a + c n)$ 的不动点迭代。其不动点满足 $a + c n^* = t$，因此 $n^* = (t - a)/c$，且"

#: manual/design/runner.md:121
msgid "The iteration contracts with rate $a/t$ near $n^*$. In fact the gap obeys an exact identity: for $n < n^*$,"
msgstr "在 $n^*$ 附近，该迭代以速率 $a/t$ 收缩。事实上，差距满足一个精确的恒等式：对于 $n < n^*$，"

#: manual/design/runner.md:133
msgid "Since $0 < a < T(n) < t$ while the loop runs, $n < f(n) < n^*$: the iteration approaches $n^*$ from below without overshooting (up to the rounding by $\\lceil\\cdot\\rceil$), and each retry multiplies the remaining gap by $a/T(n_j)$. That factor is close to $1$ while the fixed cost dominates a small batch, and falls to $a/t$ as $T(n_j)$ approaches the target: when the fixed cost is 10 % of the target, the last retries reduce the gap about tenfold each. If $a \\ge t$ there is no fixed point, and the batch grows until `max_batch_iterations` or `max_sample_time_us` stops it. Because every step increases $n$ by at least one and $n$ is capped by $n_{\\max} = \\max(\\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1)$, the loop terminates after at most $n_{\\max} - n_0$ retries."
msgstr "由于循环运行期间 $0 < a < T(n) < t$，有 $n < f(n) < n^*$：迭代从下方逼近 $n^*$ 而不会越过（除去 $\\lceil\\cdot\\rceil$ 的舍入），并且每次重试都把剩余差距乘以 $a/T(n_j)$。当固定开销主导一个小批次时，这个因子接近 $1$；随着 $T(n_j)$ 接近目标，它降到 $a/t$：当固定开销为目标的 10 % 时，最后几次重试每次大约把差距缩小十倍。如果 $a \\ge t$，则不存在不动点，批次会一直增大，直到被 `max_batch_iterations` 或 `max_sample_time_us` 阻止。由于每一步至少把 $n$ 增加一，并且 $n$ 以 $n_{\\max} = \\max(\\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations}, 1)$ 为上限，循环至多重试 $n_{\\max} - n_0$ 次后终止。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:145
msgid "With the `QuickCheck` preset ($t = 1000$ µs) and a 1 µs timer, the quantization error $\\rho / T(n)$ of a batch that reached the target is at most $0.1\\,\\%$; a batch stopped early by `max_batch_iterations` or `max_sample_time_us` can be shorter, and its `CalibrationEvent` shows it. In the browser, `performance.now()` may be coarsened to 100 µs or more; raise the target accordingly."
msgstr "使用 `QuickCheck` 预设（$t = 1000$ µs）和 1 µs 的计时器时，达到目标的批次的量化误差 $\\rho / T(n)$ 至多为 $0.1\\,\\%$；被 `max_batch_iterations` 或 `max_sample_time_us` 提前截止的批次可能更短，其 `CalibrationEvent` 会显示这一点。在浏览器中，`performance.now()` 的精度可能被降低到 100 µs 或更粗；请相应提高目标值。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:154
msgid "Validate before timing"
msgstr "先验证再计时"

#: manual/design/runner.md:156
msgid "*Problem.* A fast wrong answer must not look like a speedup. *Options.* Validate inside the timed loop; validate afterwards; validate before. *Choice.* For every dataset the runner first runs a validation sequence of `sequence_length` operations per implementation, from a fresh `clone_input`/`prepare` and `initial_context`, and compares it with the oracle. Timing starts only afterwards. *Why.* Validation inside timing would be timed; validation afterwards could not show the failing input next to the measurement. The sequence threads `next_context` from step to step, so stateful operations (an accumulator, a rounding mode, a parser state) are validated in the same order in which they are measured."
msgstr "*问题。* 一个又快又错的答案绝不能看起来像是加速。*方案。* 在计时循环内验证；事后验证；事先验证。*选择。* 对每个数据集，运行器先从新的 `clone_input`/`prepare` 和 `initial_context` 出发，为每个实现运行一个包含 `sequence_length` 次操作的验证序列，并与判定器比较。之后才开始计时。*理由。* 在计时内验证会把验证也计入时间；事后验证则无法把失败的输入展示在测量旁边。序列在步骤之间传递 `next_context`，因此有状态的操作（累加器、舍入模式、解析器状态）会按照与测量时相同的顺序被验证。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:167
msgid "Before calling the oracle, the runner maps execution outcomes that are not values:"
msgstr "在调用判定器之前，运行器会对不是值的执行结果进行如下映射："

#: manual/design/runner.md:170
msgid "Outcome of the implementation"
msgstr "实现的结果"

#: manual/design/runner.md:170
msgid "Validation status"
msgstr "验证状态"

#: manual/design/runner.md:175
msgid "decided by the oracle"
msgstr "由判定器决定"

#: manual/design/runner.md:177
msgid "For a relational oracle every unordered pair $i < j$ of implementations is compared step by step; the event is attributed to the second implementation of the pair. A sequence that ends early (`next_context = None`) is compared on the steps both sides produced. `Invalid` and `InfrastructureFailure` count as failures; a failure triggers the shrinker, if one is configured, and emits a `ValidationFailure` with the seed, both fingerprints, the shrink path and the minimal input."
msgstr "对于关系判定器，每个无序实现对 $i < j$ 都会逐步比较；事件归于该对中的第二个实现。提前结束的序列（`next_context = None`）只在双方都产生了结果的步骤上比较。`Invalid` 和 `InfrastructureFailure` 计为失败；失败会触发缩减器（若已配置），并发出一个带有种子、两个指纹、缩减路径和最小输入的 `ValidationFailure`。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:185
msgid "A failure does not stop the measurement. The report removes the series of the failing implementation for that dataset and shows the mismatch instead."
msgstr "失败不会中止测量。报告会移除失败实现在该数据集上的系列，并改为显示不匹配。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:188
msgid "Balanced, seeded rotation instead of randomization"
msgstr "平衡的、带种子的轮换，而非随机化"

#: manual/design/runner.md:190
msgid "*Problem.* Position and drift effects bias a fixed order. *Options.* Fixed order; an independent random permutation per block; a cyclic Latin square. *Choice.* The cyclic rotation derived above, with a seeded offset. *Why.* A random permutation balances positions only in expectation; with ten blocks and three implementations, one implementation can easily run first four times. The rotation balances them exactly over every cycle, and the seed still decides which implementation starts."
msgstr "*问题。* 位置效应和漂移效应会使固定顺序产生偏差。*方案。* 固定顺序；每个区组一个独立的随机排列；循环拉丁方。*选择。* 上文推导的循环轮换，加上带种子的偏移量。*理由。* 随机排列只在期望意义上平衡位置；在十个区组和三个实现的情况下，某个实现很容易有四次排在第一。轮换在每个周期上都精确地平衡位置，而种子仍决定由哪个实现开始。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:198
msgid "Calibrated batches, and one size per implementation by default"
msgstr "校准批次，默认每个实现各自一个批次大小"

#: manual/design/runner.md:200
msgid "*Problem.* Single operations are too short to time. *Choice.* Every implementation is calibrated separately (`BatchPolicy::PerImplementation`), so each reaches the target duration. `BatchPolicy::SharedBatchSize` replaces all sizes with their minimum, $n = \\min_i n_i$, for experiments in which the amount of work per batch must be identical, at the cost of a shorter batch, and a larger relative timer error, for the slower implementations. The per-iteration value $\\hat T / n$ is a batch mean: a batch reduces the variance of independent per-iteration noise by a factor $n$ but also hides the tail inside the batch."
msgstr "*问题。* 单次操作太短，无法计时。*选择。* 每个实现分别校准（`BatchPolicy::PerImplementation`），使每个实现都达到目标时长。对于每批次工作量必须完全相同的实验，`BatchPolicy::SharedBatchSize` 把所有批次大小替换为其中的最小值 $n = \\min_i n_i$，代价是较慢的实现的批次更短、相对计时误差更大。每次迭代的值 $\\hat T / n$ 是一个批次均值：批次把独立的每次迭代噪声的方差缩小 $n$ 倍，但也把批次内部的尾部掩盖了。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:209
msgid "Explicit timing boundaries"
msgstr "显式的计时边界"

#: manual/design/runner.md:211
msgid "The clock is `@bench.monotonic_clock_start`/`monotonic_clock_end` (µs). What it encloses depends on the fixture's `SetupPolicy`:"
msgstr "时钟是 `@bench.monotonic_clock_start`/`monotonic_clock_end`（µs）。它包住哪些内容取决于夹具的 `SetupPolicy`："

#: manual/design/runner.md:214
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "准备"

#: manual/design/runner.md:216
msgid "prepare once and cache; per batch: start, $n \\times$ (execute, fold), stop"
msgstr "准备一次并缓存；每个批次：启动，$n \\times$（执行，折叠），停止"

#: manual/design/runner.md:216
msgid "as excluded, except that the one-time prepare falls inside the timed region of the first batch that runs (usually a warmup batch)"
msgstr "与排除时相同，只是那一次性的准备会落在第一个运行的批次（通常是预热批次）的计时区域内"

#: manual/design/runner.md:217
msgid "prepare; start; $n \\times$ (execute, fold); stop; reset"
msgstr "准备；启动；$n \\times$（执行，折叠）；停止；重置"

#: manual/design/runner.md:217
msgid "start; prepare; $n \\times$ (execute, fold); reset; stop"
msgstr "启动；准备；$n \\times$（执行，折叠）；重置；停止"

#: manual/design/runner.md:218
msgid "$n \\times$ (prepare; start; execute; fold; stop; reset), times summed"
msgstr "$n \\times$（准备；启动；执行；折叠；停止；重置），时间求和"

#: manual/design/runner.md:218
msgid "start; $n \\times$ (prepare; execute; fold; reset); stop"
msgstr "启动；$n \\times$（准备；执行；折叠；重置）；停止"

#: manual/design/runner.md:220
msgid "`prepare` here includes `clone_input`. `synchronize` is called immediately before every start and before every stop. `finish` of the output sink and `@bench.Bench::keep` run after the stop, outside timing; `keep` stops the compiler from removing work whose result is unused. Event emission never happens inside a timed region."
msgstr "这里的 `prepare` 包含 `clone_input`。`synchronize` 在每次启动之前和每次停止之前立即调用。输出接收器的 `finish` 和 `@bench.Bench::keep` 在停止之后、计时之外运行；`keep` 阻止编译器移除结果未被使用的工作。事件发出从不发生在计时区域内。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:226
msgid "`PerIteration` with excluded setup has a cost: it takes $n$ timer readings per batch, so the quantization error is $n\\rho / (n c) = \\rho / c$ and does not shrink with the batch size. Use it only for operations that are long compared with the timer resolution."
msgstr "排除准备工作的 `PerIteration` 是有代价的：它每个批次读取 $n$ 次计时器，因此量化误差为 $n\\rho / (n c) = \\rho / c$，不会随批次大小而减小。只对相比计时器分辨率很长的操作使用它。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:231
msgid "Fixture lifecycle and sentinel sample ids"
msgstr "夹具生命周期与哨兵样本 id"

#: manual/design/runner.md:233
msgid "The fixture's `prepare` and `reset` receive a `SampleContext` or `ResetContext` whose `sample_id` tells the fixture what the runner is doing:"
msgstr "夹具的 `prepare` 和 `reset` 会收到一个 `SampleContext` 或 `ResetContext`，其 `sample_id` 告诉夹具运行器正在做什么："

#: manual/design/runner.md:236
msgid "Phase"
msgstr "阶段"

#: manual/design/runner.md:238
msgid "validation sequence"
msgstr "验证序列"

#: manual/design/runner.md:239
msgid "warmup batch $w$"
msgstr "预热批次 $w$"

#: manual/design/runner.md:240
msgid "reset after warmup (long-lived setups only)"
msgstr "预热后的重置（仅限长期存活的准备）"

#: manual/design/runner.md:241
msgid "calibration batch after $r$ retries; `-2` is also the reset after calibration"
msgstr "经过 $r$ 次重试后的校准批次；`-2` 也用于校准后的重置"

#: manual/design/runner.md:242
msgid "exploratory block $r$"
msgstr "探索性区组 $r$"

#: manual/design/runner.md:243
msgid "confirmatory block $r$"
msgstr "验证性区组 $r$"

#: manual/design/runner.md:244
msgid "final reset of a cached prepared value"
msgstr "对缓存的准备值进行最终重置"

#: manual/design/runner.md:246
msgid "Long-lived setups (`PerRun`, `PerDataset`, `PerImplementation`) are prepared once per implementation and dataset, reset after warmup and after calibration, and reset again at the end of the dataset. The runner keeps one cache per implementation, so `PerRun` and `PerDataset` currently behave like `PerImplementation`."
msgstr "长期存活的准备（`PerRun`、`PerDataset`、`PerImplementation`）对每个实现和数据集准备一次，在预热后和校准后重置，并在数据集结束时再次重置。运行器为每个实现保留一个缓存，因此 `PerRun` 和 `PerDataset` 目前的行为与 `PerImplementation` 相同。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:252
msgid "Warmup"
msgstr "预热"

#: manual/design/runner.md:254
msgid "Every implementation runs single-iteration batches until it has run `warmup_iterations` batches and spent `warmup_time_us`, capped at $\\max(\\text{warmup\\_iterations}, \\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations})$ batches. The same warmup applies to every implementation, so none starts the measurement with an advantage from just-in-time compilation or caches."
msgstr "每个实现都运行单次迭代的批次，直到它运行了 `warmup_iterations` 个批次并花费了 `warmup_time_us`，批次数上限为 $\\max(\\text{warmup\\_iterations}, \\text{max\\_batch\\_iterations})$。每个实现都适用同样的预热，因此没有哪个实现会因即时编译或缓存而在测量开始时占得优势。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:260
msgid "Crash isolation through subprocess workers"
msgstr "通过子进程工作者隔离崩溃"

#: manual/design/runner.md:262
msgid "*Problem.* A candidate that segfaults or loops forever would end the experiment. *Choice.* `Implementation::worker` runs each operation as a child process inside a task group with a hard-cancel handler, captures stdout and stderr concurrently, and turns a timeout or non-zero exit into an outcome. *Why.* An outcome is data: it is counted, reported and replayable. Process creation is part of the measured operation for workers, which is acceptable for correctness corpora and unsafe code, not for micro-benchmarks."
msgstr "*问题。* 一个段错误或陷入死循环的候选会终止整个实验。*选择。* `Implementation::worker` 把每次操作作为子进程运行在一个带强制取消处理器的任务组中，并发地捕获 stdout 和 stderr，并把超时或非零退出转化为一个结果。*理由。* 结果是数据：它会被计数、报告，并且可以重放。对工作者而言，进程创建是被测操作的一部分，这对正确性语料和不安全代码是可以接受的，但不适用于微基准测试。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:270
msgid "Seeds and identities"
msgstr "种子与身份"

#: manual/design/runner.md:272
msgid "The run seed reaches the fixture unchanged in `GenerationContext(seed, \"default\", case_id, DatasetKey(scale, index), fixture.id, fixture.version)`. Derive per-dataset seeds from it with `@generator.derive_seed`; the [generator design](generator.md) explains the mixing. The same seed sets the rotation offset. Together with the protocol, the plan and the environment snapshot, the seed determines everything except the timings."
msgstr "运行种子原样通过 `GenerationContext(seed, \"default\", case_id, DatasetKey(scale, index), fixture.id, fixture.version)` 到达夹具。请用 `@generator.derive_seed` 从它派生每个数据集的种子；[generator 设计](generator.md)解释了混合方式。同一个种子也设定轮换偏移量。种子与协议、计划和环境快照一起，决定了除计时以外的一切。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:281
msgid "**Validation precedes timing** for every dataset and implementation."
msgstr "对每个数据集和实现，**验证先于计时**。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:282
msgid "**Balance.** Over every $k$ consecutive blocks each implementation occupies each position once (proved above)."
msgstr "**平衡性。** 在每 $k$ 个连续区组中，每个实现在每个位置恰好出现一次（上文已证明）。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:284
msgid "**Event order per dataset.** Validations and failures, then one calibration event per implementation, then $k(E + C)$ observations (exploratory first); the summary is emitted once, after the last dataset."
msgstr "**每个数据集内的事件顺序。** 先是验证和失败，然后每个实现一个校准事件，然后是 $k(E + C)$ 个观测（探索性在前）；摘要在最后一个数据集之后发出一次。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:287
msgid "**Counts.** `observation_count` $= \\lvert\\text{scales}\\rvert\\cdot k (E + C)$; `calibration_count` $= \\lvert\\text{scales}\\rvert \\cdot k$; `validation_count` is the number of compared steps."
msgstr "**计数。** `observation_count` $= \\lvert\\text{scales}\\rvert\\cdot k (E + C)$；`calibration_count` $= \\lvert\\text{scales}\\rvert \\cdot k$；`validation_count` 是被比较的步骤数。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:290
msgid "**Validity.** An observation is `valid = false` when an operation in its batch produced no value or ended the context sequence."
msgstr "**有效性。** 当批次中的某次操作没有产生值或结束了上下文序列时，该观测为 `valid = false`。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:292
msgid "**Termination.** Calibration performs at most $n_{\\max} - n_0$ retries; warmup at most $\\max(\\text{warmup\\_iterations}, n_{\\max})$ batches; shrinking at most `max_steps` candidate evaluations."
msgstr "**终止性。** 校准最多进行 $n_{\\max} - n_0$ 次重试；预热最多 $\\max(\\text{warmup\\_iterations}, n_{\\max})$ 个批次；缩减最多 `max_steps` 次候选求值。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:295
msgid "**Reset discipline.** A short-lived prepared value (validation sequence, `PerSample`, `PerBatch`, `PerIteration`) is reset exactly once. A cached long-lived value is reset after warmup, after calibration and at the end of the dataset, and reused in between, so `reset` must leave it reusable."
msgstr "**重置规范。** 短期存活的准备值（验证序列、`PerSample`、`PerBatch`、`PerIteration`）恰好被重置一次。缓存的长期存活值在预热后、校准后以及数据集结束时被重置，其间被复用，因此 `reset` 必须让它保持可复用。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:302
msgid "**Random permutation per block.** Balanced only in expectation."
msgstr "**每个区组一个随机排列。** 只在期望意义上平衡。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:303
msgid "**Williams designs.** They also balance first-order carryover (which implementation ran just before), but need $2k$ blocks per cycle for odd $k$. The cyclic order always places implementation $i - 1$ before $i$ inside a block."
msgstr "**Williams 设计。** 它们还能平衡一阶残留效应（哪个实现刚刚在前面运行过），但对奇数 $k$ 每个周期需要 $2k$ 个区组。循环顺序在区组内总是把实现 $i - 1$ 放在 $i$ 之前。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:307
msgid "**Timing each iteration.** Timer overhead and resolution dominate short operations; batches amortize them."
msgstr "**为每次迭代计时。** 对短操作而言，计时器开销和分辨率会占主导；批次可以将其摊销。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:309
msgid "**Stopping when an interval is narrow enough.** Sequential stopping rules invalidate fixed-sample intervals; the sample counts are fixed by the protocol."
msgstr "**区间足够窄时停止。** 序贯停止规则会使固定样本区间失效；样本数由协议固定。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:312
msgid "**Validation after timing.** It would separate a wrong result from the measurement that should be discarded."
msgstr "**计时之后再验证。** 这会把错误的结果与本应被丢弃的测量分开。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:317
msgid "The runner does not pin threads, fix CPU frequency or isolate the process; it records what you declare about them in the `EnvironmentSnapshot`."
msgstr "运行器不绑定线程、不固定 CPU 频率，也不隔离进程；它在 `EnvironmentSnapshot` 中记录你对这些方面的声明。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:319
msgid "`experiment_design`, `outlier_policy`, `validation_coverage` and `practical_delta_pct` are stored in the protocol but do not change the run. Validation runs once per dataset, before timing, whatever the coverage says."
msgstr "`experiment_design`、`outlier_policy`、`validation_coverage` 和 `practical_delta_pct` 存储在协议中，但不会改变运行。无论覆盖率如何设置，验证都在计时之前对每个数据集运行一次。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:322
msgid "It does not compute comparisons or decisions; `stats` does."
msgstr "它不计算比较或决策；那是 `stats` 的工作。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:323
msgid "It materializes one input per scale; it does not regenerate inputs per block."
msgstr "它为每个规模物化一个输入；不会为每个区组重新生成输入。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:324
msgid "`protocol_identity`, and hence `run_id`, covers only the warmup count, the confirmatory sample count and the practical threshold."
msgstr "`protocol_identity`（进而 `run_id`）只涵盖预热次数、验证性样本数和实际阈值。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:326
msgid "Subprocess workers need the native target; `run` itself needs an async runtime (native, JS or wasm, not wasm-gc)."
msgstr "子进程工作者需要 native 目标；`run` 本身需要异步运行时（native、JS 或 wasm，不支持 wasm-gc）。"

#: manual/design/runner.md:328
msgid "First-order carryover between implementations is not balanced."
msgstr "实现之间的一阶残留效应没有被平衡。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:1
msgid "stats design"
msgstr "stats 设计"

#: manual/design/stats.md:5
msgid "Benchmark timings are skewed, heavy-tailed and correlated with the moment they were taken. `stats` gives decisions that survive these properties: robust location estimates, comparisons on paired measurements, an explicit practical threshold, and an interval whose randomness is pinned by a seed. Every function is a pure transformation of arrays, so a decision can be recomputed from the raw observations kept in the event stream."
msgstr "基准测试计时是偏斜的、重尾的，并且与采集时刻相关。`stats` 给出能经受这些性质考验的决策：稳健的位置估计、基于成对测量的比较、显式的实际阈值，以及随机性由种子固定的区间。每个函数都是数组的纯变换，因此决策可以从事件流中保存的原始观测重新计算。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:14
msgid "Timings are skewed and heavy-tailed, with a hard lower bound and rare large outliers."
msgstr "计时数据是偏斜且重尾的，有一个硬下界，偶尔出现很大的离群值。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:16
msgid "A benchmark has few blocks, often fewer than ten pairs per comparison."
msgstr "一次基准测试的区组很少，每次比较的配对常常不到十个。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:17
msgid "Every result must be recomputable from the raw observations and identical on every target."
msgstr "每个结果都必须能从原始观测重新计算，并在每个目标上完全相同。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:19
msgid "The functions take flat arrays; pairing and phase selection happen before they are called."
msgstr "这些函数接受扁平数组；配对和阶段选择在调用它们之前完成。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:24
msgid "Order statistics and the sample quantile"
msgstr "顺序统计量与样本分位数"

#: manual/design/stats.md:26
msgid "Let $x_1, \\dots, x_n$ be a sample and $x_{(1)} \\le \\dots \\le x_{(n)}$ its order statistics. The package uses one quantile definition everywhere, the linear interpolation of Hyndman and Fan's type 7:[^hf]"
msgstr "设 $x_1, \\dots, x_n$ 为样本，$x_{(1)} \\le \\dots \\le x_{(n)}$ 为其顺序统计量。本包在所有地方都使用同一个分位数定义，即 Hyndman 和 Fan 第 7 型的线性插值：[^hf]"

#: manual/design/stats.md:35
msgid "R. J. Hyndman and Y. Fan, \"Sample quantiles in statistical packages\", *The American Statistician* 50(4), 1996. Type 7 is the default of R and NumPy."
msgstr "R. J. Hyndman 和 Y. Fan，\"Sample quantiles in statistical packages\"，*The American Statistician* 50(4)，1996。第 7 型是 R 和 NumPy 的默认定义。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:37
msgid "Three properties follow directly from the formula and are used below."
msgstr "由该公式直接得到以下三个性质，下文会用到它们。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:39
msgid "**Range.** $Q(p)$ is a convex combination of two adjacent order statistics, so $x_{(1)} \\le Q(p) \\le x_{(n)}$, with $Q(0) = x_{(1)}$ and $Q(1) = x_{(n)}$."
msgstr "**范围。** $Q(p)$ 是两个相邻顺序统计量的凸组合，因此 $x_{(1)} \\le Q(p) \\le x_{(n)}$，且 $Q(0) = x_{(1)}$、$Q(1) = x_{(n)}$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:41
msgid "**Monotonicity.** $Q$ is the piecewise linear interpolation of the non-decreasing sequence $x_{(1)}, \\dots, x_{(n)}$ at the nodes $p = k/(n-1)$, so $p \\le p'$ implies $Q(p) \\le Q(p')$."
msgstr "**单调性。** $Q$ 是非递减序列 $x_{(1)}, \\dots, x_{(n)}$ 在节点 $p = k/(n-1)$ 处的分段线性插值，因此 $p \\le p'$ 蕴含 $Q(p) \\le Q(p')$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:44
msgid "**Affine equivariance.** For $y_i = a + b\\,x_i$ with $b > 0$, sorting commutes with the map and convex combinations commute with affine maps, so $Q_y(p) = a + b\\,Q_x(p)$. Rescaling timings from µs to ns rescales every quantile, median, IQR and MAD by the same factor."
msgstr "**仿射同变性。** 对于 $y_i = a + b\\,x_i$（$b > 0$），排序与该映射可交换，凸组合与仿射映射可交换，因此 $Q_y(p) = a + b\\,Q_x(p)$。把计时从 µs 换算为 ns，会使每个分位数、中位数、IQR 和 MAD 按同一因子缩放。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:49
msgid "When $h$ is an integer the second term vanishes, so $x_{(\\lfloor h\\rfloor+2)}$ is never read past the end of the sample (at $p = 1$, $h = n-1$). For an empty sample the implementation returns $0$ instead of a quantile; `summarize` makes that visible through `count == 0`."
msgstr "当 $h$ 为整数时第二项为零，因此永远不会越过样本末尾读取 $x_{(\\lfloor h\\rfloor+2)}$（在 $p = 1$ 时 $h = n-1$）。对于空样本，实现返回 $0$ 而不是分位数；`summarize` 通过 `count == 0` 让这一点可见。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:54
msgid "For $p = 1/2$ the formula gives the usual median: $x_{(m+1)}$ for $n = 2m+1$, and $\\tfrac12(x_{(m)} + x_{(m+1)})$ for $n = 2m$."
msgstr "当 $p = 1/2$ 时，公式给出通常的中位数：$n = 2m+1$ 时为 $x_{(m+1)}$，$n = 2m$ 时为 $\\tfrac12(x_{(m)} + x_{(m+1)})$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:57
msgid "Location and spread"
msgstr "位置与离散程度"

#: manual/design/stats.md:59
msgid "`summarize` reports two families of estimators side by side:"
msgstr "`summarize` 并列报告两类估计量："

#: manual/design/stats.md:61
msgid "Classical"
msgstr "经典估计量"

#: manual/design/stats.md:61
msgid "Robust"
msgstr "稳健估计量"

#: manual/design/stats.md:66
msgid "The breakdown point of an estimator is the largest fraction of the sample that can be moved arbitrarily far without moving the estimate arbitrarily far. It is $0$ for $\\bar x$ and $s_n$ (one value suffices), $1/4$ for the quartiles and the IQR, and $1/2$ for the median and the MAD. A single descheduled run moves the mean of a benchmark; it cannot move the median unless half of the runs are affected."
msgstr "估计量的崩溃点是指：样本中可以被任意远地移动、而估计值不会因此被任意远地移动的最大比例。对 $\\bar x$ 和 $s_n$ 它为 $0$（一个值就够了），对四分位数和 IQR 为 $1/4$，对中位数和 MAD 为 $1/2$。一次被调度出去的运行就能移动基准测试的均值；除非一半的运行都受到影响，否则它无法移动中位数。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:73
msgid "$s_n$ divides by $n$: it is the standard deviation of the sample viewed as a population, a descriptive quantity. As an estimator of $\\sigma^2$ it is biased, because"
msgstr "$s_n$ 除以 $n$：它是把样本视为总体时的标准差，是一个描述性的量。作为 $\\sigma^2$ 的估计量它是有偏的，因为"

#: manual/design/stats.md:84
msgid "so $\\mathbb E[s_n^2] = \\frac{n-1}{n}\\sigma^2$. Multiply $s_n^2$ by $n/(n-1)$ when you need the unbiased variance."
msgstr "所以 $\\mathbb E[s_n^2] = \\frac{n-1}{n}\\sigma^2$。需要无偏方差时，请把 $s_n^2$ 乘以 $n/(n-1)$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:87
msgid "The MAD is reported unscaled. For normally distributed data with standard deviation $\\sigma$, $\\operatorname{med}\\lvert X - \\mu\\rvert = z_{3/4}\\,\\sigma$ with $z_{3/4} = \\Phi^{-1}(3/4) \\approx 0.6745$, so $1.4826\\cdot\\mathrm{MAD}$ estimates $\\sigma$ and $\\mathrm{IQR} \\approx 1.349\\,\\sigma$."
msgstr "MAD 以未缩放的形式报告。对于标准差为 $\\sigma$ 的正态分布数据，$\\operatorname{med}\\lvert X - \\mu\\rvert = z_{3/4}\\,\\sigma$，其中 $z_{3/4} = \\Phi^{-1}(3/4) \\approx 0.6745$，因此 $1.4826\\cdot\\mathrm{MAD}$ 是 $\\sigma$ 的估计，且 $\\mathrm{IQR} \\approx 1.349\\,\\sigma$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:92
msgid "Paired measurements"
msgstr "成对测量"

#: manual/design/stats.md:94
msgid "The runner measures every implementation once per block, in a rotated order (see the [runner design](runner.md)). Model a baseline timing $b_i$ and a candidate timing $c_i$ from block $i$ as"
msgstr "运行器在每个区组中按轮换的顺序对每个实现测量一次（参见 [runner 设计](runner.md)）。把来自区组 $i$ 的基线计时 $b_i$ 和候选计时 $c_i$ 建模为"

#: manual/design/stats.md:102
msgid "where $\\beta_i$ is the block effect shared by both (machine state, frequency, cache contents) with variance $\\sigma_\\beta^2$, and $\\varepsilon_i$, $\\eta_i$ are independent noise with variances $\\sigma_\\varepsilon^2$, $\\sigma_\\eta^2$. The paired delta cancels the block effect:"
msgstr "其中 $\\beta_i$ 是两者共享的区组效应（机器状态、频率、缓存内容），方差为 $\\sigma_\\beta^2$，$\\varepsilon_i$、$\\eta_i$ 是相互独立的噪声，方差分别为 $\\sigma_\\varepsilon^2$、$\\sigma_\\eta^2$。成对差值抵消了区组效应："

#: manual/design/stats.md:112
msgid ""
"whereas a difference taken across blocks $i \\n"
"e j$ has variance $\\sigma_\\varepsilon^2 + \\sigma_\\eta^2 + 2\\sigma_\\beta^2$. When drift between blocks dominates the noise inside a block, pairing removes most of the variance. `compare_paired` therefore takes the location of the deltas, $\\operatorname{med}(d)$, and never the difference $\\operatorname{med}(c) - \\operatorname{med}(b)$ of two separate locations; the baseline median enters only as the scale of the relative delta."
msgstr ""
"而跨区组 $i \\n"
"e j$ 取的差值方差为 $\\sigma_\\varepsilon^2 + \\sigma_\\eta^2 + 2\\sigma_\\beta^2$。当区组间的漂移比区组内的噪声更占主导时，配对能消除大部分方差。因此 `compare_paired` 取的是差值的位置 $\\operatorname{med}(d)$，而从不取两个各自位置之差 $\\operatorname{med}(c) - \\operatorname{med}(b)$；基线中位数只作为相对差值的尺度出现。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:120
msgid "The percentile bootstrap"
msgstr "百分位自助法"

#: manual/design/stats.md:122
msgid "Let $\\hat F_n$ be the empirical distribution of the deltas and $\\hat\\theta = \\operatorname{med}(d)$. A bootstrap resample $d^*$ draws $n$ values from $\\hat F_n$ with replacement; its median is $\\hat\\theta^*$. Write $\\hat G(x) = P^*(\\hat\\theta^* \\le x)$ for the bootstrap distribution. The percentile interval at confidence $1-\\alpha$ is"
msgstr "设 $\\hat F_n$ 为差值的经验分布，$\\hat\\theta = \\operatorname{med}(d)$。一个自助法重抽样样本 $d^*$ 从 $\\hat F_n$ 中有放回地抽取 $n$ 个值；其中位数为 $\\hat\\theta^*$。把自助法分布记作 $\\hat G(x) = P^*(\\hat\\theta^* \\le x)$。置信度为 $1-\\alpha$ 的百分位区间为"

#: manual/design/stats.md:132
msgid "It is exact under the following condition. Suppose an increasing map $\\varphi$ exists such that $W = \\varphi(\\hat\\theta) - \\varphi(\\theta)$ has a distribution $H$ symmetric about $0$, and the same $H$ describes $\\varphi(\\hat\\theta^*) - \\varphi(\\hat\\theta)$ under resampling. Then $\\hat G^{-1}(q) = \\varphi^{-1}\\bigl(\\varphi(\\hat\\theta) + H^{-1}(q)\\bigr)$ and"
msgstr "在下述条件下它是精确的。假设存在一个递增映射 $\\varphi$，使得 $W = \\varphi(\\hat\\theta) - \\varphi(\\theta)$ 具有关于 $0$ 对称的分布 $H$，并且在重抽样下同一个 $H$ 也描述 $\\varphi(\\hat\\theta^*) - \\varphi(\\hat\\theta)$。那么 $\\hat G^{-1}(q) = \\varphi^{-1}\\bigl(\\varphi(\\hat\\theta) + H^{-1}(q)\\bigr)$，且"

#: manual/design/stats.md:149
msgid "using $H^{-1}(q) = -H^{-1}(1-q)$. For a continuous $H$ the coverage is $P\\bigl(H^{-1}(\\alpha/2) \\le W \\le H^{-1}(1-\\alpha/2)\\bigr) = 1-\\alpha$. The interval never needs to know $\\varphi$, which is why it is transformation-respecting.[^et]"
msgstr "这里用到了 $H^{-1}(q) = -H^{-1}(1-q)$。对于连续的 $H$，覆盖率为 $P\\bigl(H^{-1}(\\alpha/2) \\le W \\le H^{-1}(1-\\alpha/2)\\bigr) = 1-\\alpha$。该区间从不需要知道 $\\varphi$，这就是它具有变换保持性的原因。[^et]"

#: manual/design/stats.md:154
msgid "In general the condition holds only approximately. For smooth statistics (means and smooth functions of means) Edgeworth expansions give the size of the error: each one-sided percentile bound misses its nominal tail probability by $O(n^{-1/2})$, and in the two-sided equal-tailed interval these leading terms cancel, leaving a coverage error of $O(n^{-1})$.[^hall] The median is not a smooth statistic: its bootstrap distribution is discrete (derived next), the expansions do not apply, and for the small $n$ of a benchmark the error is dominated by that discreteness."
msgstr "一般情况下该条件只是近似成立。对于光滑统计量（均值以及均值的光滑函数），Edgeworth 展开给出了误差的大小：每个单侧百分位界与其名义尾部概率相差 $O(n^{-1/2})$，而在双侧等尾区间中这些主导项相互抵消，留下 $O(n^{-1})$ 的覆盖误差。[^hall] 中位数不是光滑统计量：它的自助分布是离散的（下文推导），这些展开不适用，而对于基准测试中较小的 $n$，误差由这种离散性主导。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:163
msgid "P. Hall, *The Bootstrap and Edgeworth Expansion*, Springer, 1992, §3.5. BCa and the bootstrap-$t$ reduce the one-sided error to $O(n^{-1})$."
msgstr "P. Hall, *The Bootstrap and Edgeworth Expansion*, Springer, 1992, §3.5。BCa 和自助 $t$ 法把单侧误差降低到 $O(n^{-1})$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:165
msgid "B. Efron and R. J. Tibshirani, *An Introduction to the Bootstrap*, Chapman & Hall, 1993, §13.3 and §14."
msgstr "B. Efron 和 R. J. Tibshirani，*An Introduction to the Bootstrap*，Chapman & Hall，1993，§13.3 与 §14。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:167
msgid "For the median the bootstrap distribution can be written down exactly. Take $n = 2m+1$ distinct values. $\\hat\\theta^* \\le x_{(k)}$ holds exactly when at least $m+1$ of the $n$ draws are at most $x_{(k)}$, and each draw is with probability $k/n$, so"
msgstr "对于中位数，自助法分布可以精确写出。取 $n = 2m+1$ 个互不相同的值。$\\hat\\theta^* \\le x_{(k)}$ 恰好在 $n$ 次抽取中至少有 $m+1$ 次不超过 $x_{(k)}$ 时成立，而每次抽取满足这一点的概率为 $k/n$，因此"

#: manual/design/stats.md:176
msgid "For odd $n$, $\\hat G$ is a step function that jumps only at the data points. For even $n = 2m$ the resampled median is the midpoint of the $m$-th and $(m+1)$-th resampled order statistics, which can be any two data points, so the jumps sit at the midpoints $\\tfrac12(x_{(j)} + x_{(k)})$ with $j \\le k$, not only at midpoints of adjacent values. Either way the interval endpoints land on, or between, observed deltas, and with few blocks they move in coarse steps."
msgstr "对于奇数 $n$，$\\hat G$ 是只在数据点处跳跃的阶梯函数。对于偶数 $n = 2m$，重抽样中位数是重抽样后第 $m$ 和第 $(m+1)$ 个次序统计量的中点，而它们可以是任意两个数据点，因此跳跃位于中点 $\\tfrac12(x_{(j)} + x_{(k)})$（$j \\le k$），而不只是相邻值的中点。无论哪种情况，区间端点都落在观测到的差值上或它们之间，并且区组较少时它们以粗糙的步长移动。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:183
msgid "**Actual coverage for small $n$.** Let the deltas be independent draws from a continuous distribution with median $\\theta$, and $n$ odd. With many resamples the endpoints are order statistics, $L = d_{(i)}$ and $U = d_{(j)}$, where $i$ is the smallest $k$ with $\\hat G(d_{(k)}) \\ge \\alpha/2$ and $j$ the smallest $k$ with $\\hat G(d_{(k)}) \\ge 1-\\alpha/2$; by the formula above, $i$ and $j$ depend on $n$ and $\\alpha$ only. The number $K = \\lvert\\{\\, l : d_l \\le \\theta \\,\\}\\rvert$ of deltas at or below the median is $\\mathrm{Bin}(n, \\tfrac12)$, and $d_{(i)} \\le \\theta \\iff K \\ge i$, $\\theta < d_{(j)} \\iff K \\le j-1$, so"
msgstr "**小 $n$ 时的实际覆盖率。** 设差值是来自中位数为 $\\theta$ 的连续分布的独立抽取，且 $n$ 为奇数。当重抽样次数很多时，端点是次序统计量 $L = d_{(i)}$ 和 $U = d_{(j)}$，其中 $i$ 是满足 $\\hat G(d_{(k)}) \\ge \\alpha/2$ 的最小 $k$，$j$ 是满足 $\\hat G(d_{(k)}) \\ge 1-\\alpha/2$ 的最小 $k$；由上面的公式，$i$ 和 $j$ 只依赖于 $n$ 和 $\\alpha$。不超过中位数的差值个数 $K = \\lvert\\{\\, l : d_l \\le \\theta \\,\\}\\rvert$ 服从 $\\mathrm{Bin}(n, \\tfrac12)$，并且 $d_{(i)} \\le \\theta \\iff K \\ge i$、$\\theta < d_{(j)} \\iff K \\le j-1$，因此"

#: manual/design/stats.md:197
msgid "for every continuous distribution. For a nominal 95 % interval:"
msgstr "这对每个连续分布都成立。对于名义 95 % 的区间："

#: manual/design/stats.md:199
msgid "actual coverage"
msgstr "实际覆盖率"

#: manual/design/stats.md:208
msgid "The coverage oscillates around the nominal level and can fall well below it with a handful of blocks; it settles near 95 % only from about fifty pairs on. Treat the interval of a short run as a description of the spread of the resampled medians, not as a guarantee."
msgstr "覆盖率在名义水平附近振荡，在只有少数几个区组时可能远低于它；大约从五十个配对起它才稳定在 95 % 附近。请把短运行的区间看作对重抽样中位数分散程度的描述，而不是一种保证。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:213
msgid "The derivation of these results in full, with the discreteness bound, is in the attachment:"
msgstr "这些结果的完整推导以及离散性界见附件："

#: manual/design/stats.md:216
msgid "[Percentile bootstrap of the median paired delta](../../attachments/design_stats_bootstrap.typ)"
msgstr "[成对差值中位数的百分位自助法](../../attachments/design_stats_bootstrap.typ)"

#: manual/design/stats.md:220
msgid "Medians as the default centre"
msgstr "以中位数作为默认中心"

#: manual/design/stats.md:222
msgid "*Problem.* Timing distributions have a hard lower bound (the work itself) and a long right tail (interrupts, page faults, frequency changes). *Options.* Mean, trimmed mean, median. *Choice.* The median for every decision, with the mean kept in `SummaryStats` as a diagnostic. *Why.* Its breakdown point is $1/2$, it is affine equivariant, and the distance between mean and median signals a tail that deserves a look in the report."
msgstr "*问题。* 计时分布有一个硬性的下界（工作本身）和一条长长的右尾（中断、缺页、频率变化）。*方案。* 均值、截尾均值、中位数。*选择。* 每个决策都使用中位数，均值作为诊断量保留在 `SummaryStats` 中。*理由。* 中位数的崩溃点为 $1/2$，具有仿射同变性，而均值与中位数之间的距离提示存在值得在报告中查看的尾部。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:229
msgid "Paired deltas instead of two independent samples"
msgstr "成对差值，而非两个独立样本"

#: manual/design/stats.md:231
msgid "*Problem.* Machine state drifts between blocks. *Options.* Compare $\\operatorname{med}(c) - \\operatorname{med}(b)$; compare the paired deltas. *Choice.* `compare_paired` computes $d_i = c_i - b_i$ and summarizes $\\operatorname{med}(d)$. *Why.* The variance derivation above: the block effect cancels in $d_i$ and stays in an unpaired difference. The cost is a contract: index $i$ of both arrays must come from the same dataset, repetition and block. `paired_deltas` truncates to the shorter array and `compare_paired` marks unequal lengths `Invalid`, so a broken alignment is visible instead of being silently repaired."
msgstr "*问题。* 机器状态在区组之间漂移。*方案。* 比较 $\\operatorname{med}(c) - \\operatorname{med}(b)$；比较成对差值。*选择。* `compare_paired` 计算 $d_i = c_i - b_i$ 并总结 $\\operatorname{med}(d)$。*理由。* 见上文的方差推导：区组效应在 $d_i$ 中抵消，而在非成对差值中保留。代价是一份契约：两个数组的索引 $i$ 必须来自同一个数据集、重复和区组。`paired_deltas` 截断到较短的数组，`compare_paired` 把长度不等标记为 `Invalid`，因此对齐错误会显现出来，而不是被悄悄修补。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:241
msgid "The relative delta and the speedup"
msgstr "相对差值与加速比"

#: manual/design/stats.md:243
msgid "*Problem.* Gates are stated in percent, people read speedups. *Choice.* With $m_b = \\operatorname{med}(b)$ and $m_d = \\operatorname{med}(d)$,"
msgstr "*问题。* 门禁以百分比表述，而人们读的是加速比。*选择。* 令 $m_b = \\operatorname{med}(b)$，$m_d = \\operatorname{med}(d)$，"

#: manual/design/stats.md:251
msgid "Both are functions of the same two medians, so away from the guards below they never disagree: $s$ is decreasing in $r$ on $r > -100$, and for a threshold $0 \\le t < 100$"
msgstr "两者都是同两个中位数的函数，因此除了下面的保护条件之外，它们永远不会矛盾：在 $r > -100$ 上 $s$ 关于 $r$ 递减，对于阈值 $0 \\le t < 100$"

#: manual/design/stats.md:259
msgid ""
"A threshold of $t = 2$ declares the candidate `Faster` exactly when $s \\ge 1.0204$. When the candidate is a constant shift of the baseline, $c_i = b_i + \\delta$, then $m_b + m_d = \\operatorname{med}(c)$ and $s$ is the ratio of the medians; in general $m_b + m_d$ is a robust estimate of the typical candidate time built from the paired data. The guards $m_b = 0 \\Rightarrow r = 0$ and $m_d = 0 \\Rightarrow s = 1$ keep degenerate input finite. They break the identity $s = 1/(1 + r/100)$ in one case: with $m_b = 0$ and $m_d \\n"
"e 0$ the code reports $r = 0$ but $s = 0/m_d = 0$. A baseline whose median time is $0$ cannot be compared in relative terms; check `SummaryStats.median` first. $r = -100$ ($m_b + m_d = 0$, for example a candidate that always reports $0$) still gives an infinite speedup."
msgstr ""
"阈值 $t = 2$ 恰好在 $s \\ge 1.0204$ 时宣布候选为 `Faster`。当候选是基线的常数平移 $c_i = b_i + \\delta$ 时，$m_b + m_d = \\operatorname{med}(c)$，$s$ 就是两个中位数之比；一般而言，$m_b + m_d$ 是根据成对数据构建的典型候选时间的稳健估计。保护条件 $m_b = 0 \\Rightarrow r = 0$ 和 $m_d = 0 \\Rightarrow s = 1$ 使退化输入保持有限。它们在一种情况下破坏了恒等式 $s = 1/(1 + r/100)$：当 $m_b = 0$ 且 $m_d \\n"
"e 0$ 时，代码报告 $r = 0$，但 $s = 0/m_d = 0$。中位时间为 $0$ 的基线无法做相对比较；请先检查 `SummaryStats.median`。$r = -100$（$m_b + m_d = 0$，例如一个总是报告 $0$ 的候选）仍会给出无穷大的加速比。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:271
msgid "When the arrays have different lengths, $m_d$ comes from the $\\min(\\lvert b\\rvert, \\lvert c\\rvert)$ pairs but $m_b$ from the whole baseline; the decision is then `Invalid`, and $r$ and $s$ are not meaningful."
msgstr "当数组长度不同时，$m_d$ 来自 $\\min(\\lvert b\\rvert, \\lvert c\\rvert)$ 个配对，而 $m_b$ 来自整个基线；此时决策为 `Invalid`，$r$ 和 $s$ 没有意义。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:275
msgid "A practical threshold instead of a significance test"
msgstr "实际阈值，而非显著性检验"

#: manual/design/stats.md:277
msgid "*Problem.* With enough repetitions any difference becomes statistically significant, including a 0.1 % change nobody would act on. *Options.* A $t$-test or Wilcoxon test; an equivalence test (TOST); a practical threshold on the point estimate. *Choice.* For $t > 0$ the decision is the three-way rule"
msgstr "*问题。* 只要重复次数足够多，任何差异都会变得统计显著，包括没有人会为之行动的 0.1 % 的变化。*选项。* $t$ 检验或 Wilcoxon 检验；等价性检验（TOST）；对点估计使用实际阈值。*选择。* 对于 $t > 0$，决策是三分规则"

#: manual/design/stats.md:288
msgid "checked after `Invalid` (unequal lengths) and `Unknown` (no pairs). *Why.* The threshold states the question the user is asking (\"is it at least 2 % faster?\") in the unit of the decision, the rule is reproducible from two medians, and it does not reward running more repetitions. Uncertainty is reported next to the decision through the interval, not folded into it."
msgstr "在 `Invalid`（长度不等）和 `Unknown`（没有配对）之后检查。*理由。* 阈值以决策的单位陈述用户真正关心的问题（“它是否至少快 2 %？”），该规则可以由两个中位数复现，并且不会奖励运行更多的重复。不确定性通过区间在决策旁边报告，而不是折叠进决策中。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:294
msgid ""
"The rule is meaningful only for a threshold $t \\in [0, \\infty)$ and a relative delta $r \\n"
"e \\mathrm{NaN}$; `compare_paired` returns `Invalid` otherwise. For valid inputs the code evaluates"
msgstr ""
"这条规则只对阈值 $t \\in [0, \\infty)$ 和相对差值 $r \\n"
"e \\mathrm{NaN}$ 有意义；否则 `compare_paired` 返回 `Invalid`。对于有效输入，代码求值"

#: manual/design/stats.md:307
msgid "The sign conditions make the first two regions disjoint for every $t \\ge 0$: $\\{r < 0,\\ r \\le -t\\} = (-\\infty, -t] \\setminus \\{0\\}$ and $\\{r > 0,\\ r \\ge t\\} = [t, \\infty) \\setminus \\{0\\}$, so together with the rest of the line they partition $\\mathbb R$. For $t > 0$ the sign conditions are implied by the threshold tests and the rule is exactly the one above. For $t = 0$ they matter: an exact tie $r = 0$ lies in neither of the first two regions and is `Equivalent`, while every other $r$ is `Faster` or `Slower`. Without them, $0 \\le -0$ would make a tie `Faster`.[^issue1]"
msgstr "符号条件使前两个区域对每个 $t \\ge 0$ 都不相交：$\\{r < 0,\\ r \\le -t\\} = (-\\infty, -t] \\setminus \\{0\\}$，$\\{r > 0,\\ r \\ge t\\} = [t, \\infty) \\setminus \\{0\\}$，因此它们与实数轴的其余部分一起构成 $\\mathbb R$ 的一个划分。对于 $t > 0$，符号条件可由阈值检验推出，规则恰好就是上面那条。对于 $t = 0$ 它们很关键：完全持平 $r = 0$ 不属于前两个区域中的任何一个，因此为 `Equivalent`，而其他每个 $r$ 都是 `Faster` 或 `Slower`。没有它们，$0 \\le -0$ 会让持平变成 `Faster`。[^issue1]"

#: manual/design/stats.md:316
msgid "A threshold that is `NaN`, infinite or negative has no meaning as \"the smallest change you care about\", and every comparison with `NaN` is false, so such a threshold would silently classify everything as `Equivalent` (or, for $t < 0$, small slowdowns as `Faster`). Returning `Invalid` makes the mistake visible. `runner.validate_protocol` rejects the same thresholds before a run."
msgstr "为 `NaN`、无穷大或负数的阈值无法表示“你关心的最小变化”，而且与 `NaN` 的任何比较都为假，因此这样的阈值会悄悄地把一切归为 `Equivalent`（或者在 $t < 0$ 时把小幅变慢归为 `Faster`）。返回 `Invalid` 使这个错误变得可见。`runner.validate_protocol` 会在运行前拒绝同样的阈值。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:322
msgid "Fixed in [issue #1](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mare_mark/issues/1). `experiment.comparator_label` uses the same rule and returns `\"Unknown\"` where `compare_paired` returns `Equivalent` or `Invalid`."
msgstr "已在 [issue #1](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mare_mark/issues/1) 中修复。`experiment.comparator_label` 使用相同的规则，在 `compare_paired` 返回 `Equivalent` 或 `Invalid` 的地方返回 `\"Unknown\"`。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:324
msgid "Seeded percentile bootstrap of the median delta"
msgstr "对中位数差值的带种子百分位自助法"

#: manual/design/stats.md:326
msgid "*Problem.* A reader of a report needs to see how stable the median delta is, and the number must be the same when the report is regenerated. *Choice.* `bootstrap_interval` draws $B$ resamples with an explicit seed and returns the type-7 quantiles $Q^*(\\alpha/2)$ and $Q^*(1-\\alpha/2)$ of the $B$ resampled medians. *Why.* The percentile method needs no variance formula for the median (which would need a density estimate), it is transformation-respecting, and it is cheap: $O(B\\,n\\log n)$."
msgstr "*问题。* 报告的读者需要看到中位数差值有多稳定，而且重新生成报告时这个数字必须保持不变。*选择。* `bootstrap_interval` 用显式种子抽取 $B$ 个重抽样样本，并返回 $B$ 个重抽样中位数的第 7 型分位数 $Q^*(\\alpha/2)$ 和 $Q^*(1-\\alpha/2)$。*理由。* 百分位方法不需要中位数的方差公式（那需要密度估计），它具有变换保持性，而且代价低廉：$O(B\\,n\\log n)$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:334
msgid "The random stream is generated by a 64-bit xorshift step followed by a multiplication:"
msgstr "随机流由一个 64 位 xorshift 步骤加一次乘法生成："

#: manual/design/stats.md:344
msgid "These are the constants of Marsaglia–Vigna xorshift64\\*, but the multiplied value is fed back as the next state, so the classical period result for xorshift64\\* does not carry over. What does carry over: each xorshift step is an invertible linear map over $\\mathrm{GF}(2)^{64}$ (a unipotent triangular matrix), and multiplication by an odd constant is invertible modulo $2^{64}$, so one step is a permutation of the 64-bit words that fixes $0$. That is why seed `0` is replaced by the constant `88172645463393265`; as a consequence the seeds `0` and `88172645463393265` give the same stream. Because the step is a permutation that fixes $0$, a non-zero state never becomes $0$. The generator uses only wrapping 64-bit integer arithmetic, so the stream is identical on every target."
msgstr "这些是 Marsaglia–Vigna xorshift64\\* 的常数，但相乘后的值会作为下一个状态反馈回去，因此 xorshift64\\* 经典的周期结论并不适用。仍然适用的是：每个 xorshift 步骤都是 $\\mathrm{GF}(2)^{64}$ 上的可逆线性映射（一个幺幂三角矩阵），而乘以奇数常数在模 $2^{64}$ 下可逆，因此一步就是 64 位字上一个固定 $0$ 的置换。这就是种子 `0` 会被替换为常数 `88172645463393265` 的原因；其结果是种子 `0` 和 `88172645463393265` 给出相同的流。由于这一步是固定 $0$ 的置换，非零状态永远不会变成 $0$。生成器只使用回绕的 64 位整数算术，因此该流在每个目标上都完全相同。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:356
msgid "A state $x$ is mapped to an index by $j = x \\bmod n$. Writing $2^{64} = qn + r$ with $0 \\le r < n$, the residues $j < r$ are hit $q+1$ times and the others $q$ times, so for a uniformly distributed state"
msgstr "状态 $x$ 通过 $j = x \\bmod n$ 映射为索引。记 $2^{64} = qn + r$，其中 $0 \\le r < n$，则余数 $j < r$ 被命中 $q+1$ 次，其他余数被命中 $q$ 次，因此对于均匀分布的状态"

#: manual/design/stats.md:365
msgid "For a million deltas the bias is below $10^{-13}$, far below the Monte Carlo error of the interval."
msgstr "对于一百万个差值，偏差低于 $10^{-13}$，远低于区间的蒙特卡罗误差。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:368
msgid "*Choosing $B$.* An endpoint estimated from $B$ resampled medians has a standard error of order $\\sqrt{p(1-p)/B}$ in probability units, with $p = \\alpha/2$. For a 95 % interval and $B = 2000$ this is about $0.35$ percentage points of the 2.5 % tail mass. Use $B \\ge 1000$ for 95 % intervals and keep the seed and $B$ with the experiment configuration."
msgstr "*选择 $B$。* 由 $B$ 个重抽样中位数估计的端点，以概率单位计的标准误为 $\\sqrt{p(1-p)/B}$ 阶，其中 $p = \\alpha/2$。对于 95 % 区间和 $B = 2000$，这约为 2.5 % 尾部质量的 $0.35$ 个百分点。对 95 % 区间请使用 $B \\ge 1000$，并把种子和 $B$ 与实验配置一起保存。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:374
msgid "Outlier views instead of outlier deletion"
msgstr "离群值视图，而非删除离群值"

#: manual/design/stats.md:376
msgid "*Problem.* Reports want plots without one 50 ms page-fault spike; decisions must not depend on which points someone chose to hide. *Choice.* `filter_outliers` returns a filtered copy under an explicit `OutlierPolicy`, and nothing in the runner or the event stream applies it. *Why.* The raw data stay auditable, and the policy is a named value that can be recorded. The two non-trivial policies have known false-flag rates on clean normal data:"
msgstr "*问题。* 报告希望图表中没有那个 50 ms 的缺页尖峰；而决策不能取决于某人选择隐藏了哪些点。*选择。* `filter_outliers` 在显式的 `OutlierPolicy` 下返回过滤后的副本，运行器和事件流中都不会应用它。*理由。* 原始数据保持可审计，策略是一个可以被记录的具名值。两种非平凡策略在干净的正态数据上具有已知的误标率："

#: manual/design/stats.md:392
msgid "Because the MAD is unscaled, the MAD trim removes about six times as many points as the Tukey fence from clean normal data ($4.3\\,\\%$ against $0.70\\,\\%$). It is also degenerate when more than half of the values coincide: the MAD is then $0$ and only values equal to the median survive. Both filters compute their fences from the values that are not `NaN` and never keep a `NaN`."
msgstr "由于 MAD 未缩放，在干净的正态数据上，MAD 截尾去除的点数大约是 Tukey 围栏的六倍（$4.3\\,\\%$ 对 $0.70\\,\\%$）。当超过一半的值相同时它也会退化：此时 MAD 为 $0$，只有等于中位数的值会保留下来。两种过滤都用非 `NaN` 的值计算围栏，并且从不保留 `NaN`。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:399
msgid "`NaN` propagates"
msgstr "`NaN` 会传播"

#: manual/design/stats.md:401
msgid "*Problem.* The default `Double` order puts a `NaN` at an unspecified position of a sort, so order statistics computed after sorting a sample with a `NaN` are inconsistent (a minimum above the maximum) and depend on the position of the `NaN` in the input. *Options.* Reject `NaN` with an error; drop it silently; propagate it. *Choice.* `summarize` returns `NaN` for every statistic except `count` when the input contains a `NaN`, and `compare_paired` turns the resulting `NaN` relative delta into `Invalid`. *Why.* Both functions are total and have no error channel; propagation keeps the result honest without changing their signatures, and `count` still shows how many values were passed. Dropping values would change $n$ and the pairing silently. The bootstrap functions, which already return `Result`, keep rejecting non-finite values with `NonFiniteSample`."
msgstr "*问题。* 默认的 `Double` 顺序会把 `NaN` 放在排序中一个未规定的位置，因此对含有 `NaN` 的样本排序后计算的次序统计量彼此不一致（最小值大于最大值），并且依赖于 `NaN` 在输入中的位置。*选项。* 用错误拒绝 `NaN`；悄悄丢弃它；让它传播。*选择。* 当输入含有 `NaN` 时，`summarize` 对除 `count` 外的每个统计量都返回 `NaN`，而 `compare_paired` 把由此得到的 `NaN` 相对差值变成 `Invalid`。*理由。* 这两个函数都是全函数，没有错误通道；传播在不改变签名的前提下保持结果诚实，而 `count` 仍然显示传入了多少个值。丢弃值会悄悄改变 $n$ 和配对。已经返回 `Result` 的自助法函数继续以 `NonFiniteSample` 拒绝非有限值。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:414
msgid "Errors as values"
msgstr "错误即值"

#: manual/design/stats.md:416
msgid "Invalid bootstrap input returns `Err(BootstrapError)`. An empty or non-finite sample would otherwise yield a plausible-looking interval of zeros or `NaN`. `summarize` and `compare_paired` stay total: they return neutral values (`count == 0`, `NaN` statistics, `Unknown`, `Invalid`) that a caller can test."
msgstr "无效的自助法输入返回 `Err(BootstrapError)`。否则，空样本或非有限样本会产生一个看似合理的全零或 `NaN` 区间。`summarize` 和 `compare_paired` 保持为全函数：它们返回调用者可以检验的中性值（`count == 0`、`NaN` 统计量、`Unknown`、`Invalid`）。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:424
msgid "**Inputs are not modified.** `summarize` sorts a copy; `filter_outliers` returns a new array; the bootstrap sorts each resample, never the input."
msgstr "**输入不会被修改。** `summarize` 对副本排序；`filter_outliers` 返回新数组；自助法对每个重抽样样本排序，从不对输入排序。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:426
msgid "**Range.** By the range property of $Q$, `median`, `q1` and `q3` lie in $[x_{(1)}, x_{(n)}]$. Every resampled median lies in $[\\min d, \\max d]$ because it is a quantile of values drawn from $d$; the interval endpoints are quantiles of those medians, hence $\\min d \\le$ `low` $\\le$ `high` $\\le \\max d$."
msgstr "**范围。** 由 $Q$ 的范围性质，`median`、`q1` 和 `q3` 位于 $[x_{(1)}, x_{(n)}]$ 中。每个重抽样中位数都位于 $[\\min d, \\max d]$ 中，因为它是从 $d$ 中抽取的值的分位数；区间端点又是这些中位数的分位数，因此 $\\min d \\le$ `low` $\\le$ `high` $\\le \\max d$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:431
msgid "**Order.** For $0 < \\gamma < 100$, $\\alpha/2 < 1 - \\alpha/2$, and monotonicity of $Q$ gives `low` $\\le$ `high`."
msgstr "**顺序。** 对于 $0 < \\gamma < 100$，有 $\\alpha/2 < 1 - \\alpha/2$，由 $Q$ 的单调性得到 `low` $\\le$ `high`。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:433
msgid "**Determinism.** The bootstrap is a function of (values, seed, $B$, $\\gamma$). Sorting finite doubles is deterministic, and the generator uses wrapping integer arithmetic, so the same inputs give bit-identical bounds on every target."
msgstr "**确定性。** 自助法是（值、种子、$B$、$\\gamma$）的函数。对有限双精度数排序是确定性的，生成器使用回绕整数算术，因此相同的输入在每个目标上都给出逐位相同的边界。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:437
msgid "**Floating-point error.** The mean is a left-to-right sum. With $u = 2^{-53}$ and $\\gamma_k = ku/(1-ku)$, the standard bound $\\lvert \\mathrm{fl}(\\sum x_i) - \\sum x_i\\rvert \\le \\gamma_{n-1}\\sum \\lvert x_i\\rvert$ becomes a relative error of at most $\\gamma_{n-1} \\approx n u$ for positive timings. The variance uses the two-pass formula $\\sum (x_i - \\bar x)^2$, which avoids the cancellation of the one-pass $\\sum x_i^2 - n\\bar x^2$.[^higham]"
msgstr "**浮点误差。** 均值是从左到右的求和。令 $u = 2^{-53}$、$\\gamma_k = ku/(1-ku)$，标准界 $\\lvert \\mathrm{fl}(\\sum x_i) - \\sum x_i\\rvert \\le \\gamma_{n-1}\\sum \\lvert x_i\\rvert$ 对正的计时值而言就是至多 $\\gamma_{n-1} \\approx n u$ 的相对误差。方差使用两遍公式 $\\sum (x_i - \\bar x)^2$，避免了单遍公式 $\\sum x_i^2 - n\\bar x^2$ 的相消问题。[^higham]"

#: manual/design/stats.md:443
msgid "**Complexity.** `summarize` is $O(n\\log n)$; `compare_paired` is $O(n\\log n)$; `bootstrap_interval` is $O(B\\,n\\log n + B\\log B)$; `filter_outliers` is $O(n\\log n)$."
msgstr "**复杂度。** `summarize` 为 $O(n\\log n)$；`compare_paired` 为 $O(n\\log n)$；`bootstrap_interval` 为 $O(B\\,n\\log n + B\\log B)$；`filter_outliers` 为 $O(n\\log n)$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:447
msgid "N. J. Higham, *Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*, 2nd ed., SIAM, 2002, §4.2 and §1.9."
msgstr "N. J. Higham，*Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*，第 2 版，SIAM，2002，§4.2 与 §1.9。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:451
msgid "**BCa and studentized bootstrap.** For smooth statistics they reduce the one-sided coverage error from $O(n^{-1/2})$ to $O(n^{-1})$, but they need a jackknife acceleration estimate or a variance estimate for every resample; for the median both are unstable with the small $n$ that benchmarks have, and neither removes the discreteness derived above. Not implemented."
msgstr "**BCa 与学生化自助法。** 对于光滑统计量，它们把单侧覆盖误差从 $O(n^{-1/2})$ 降低到 $O(n^{-1})$，但需要为每个重抽样样本给出刀切法加速估计或方差估计；对于中位数，在基准测试常见的小 $n$ 下两者都不稳定，而且都不能消除上文推导的离散性。未实现。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:456
msgid "**Hierarchical bootstrap.** Resampling datasets, then repetitions, matches `HierarchicalDatasetsAndRepeats` better, but the comparison functions take flat arrays. Callers can still resample per dataset themselves."
msgstr "**分层自助法。** 先重抽样数据集、再重抽样重复，更契合 `HierarchicalDatasetsAndRepeats`，但比较函数接收的是扁平数组。调用者仍然可以自行按数据集重抽样。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:459
msgid "**Hodges–Lehmann estimator.** The median of pairwise Walsh averages is more efficient under symmetry, but costs $O(n^2)$ and is harder to explain in a report."
msgstr "**Hodges–Lehmann 估计量。** 两两 Walsh 平均的中位数在对称条件下更有效，但代价为 $O(n^2)$，且更难在报告中解释。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:462
msgid "**Hypothesis tests ($t$, Welch, Mann–Whitney).** Rejected for the decision as explained above; their $p$-values answer a different question."
msgstr "**假设检验（$t$、Welch、Mann–Whitney）。** 如上所述，不用于决策；它们的 $p$ 值回答的是另一个问题。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:464
msgid "**Scaled MAD.** Multiplying by 1.4826 assumes normality; the unscaled value is reported and the factor is documented instead."
msgstr "**缩放的 MAD。** 乘以 1.4826 隐含了正态性假设；因此报告未缩放的值，并在文档中说明该因子。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:469
msgid "The decision uses the point estimate and the threshold only; the interval is reported, not used to decide. There is no equivalence test."
msgstr "决策只使用点估计和阈值；区间被报告，但不用于决策。没有等价性检验。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:471
msgid "Comparisons take flat arrays. Pairing, phase separation (exploratory or confirmatory) and environment compatibility are the caller's job."
msgstr "比较函数接收扁平数组。配对、阶段划分（探索性或验证性）和环境兼容性由调用者负责。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:473
msgid "The bootstrap interval is in the unit of the deltas; the decision is in percent. Divide by $\\operatorname{med}(b)$ to compare them."
msgstr "自助法区间的单位与差值相同；决策以百分比表示。要比较两者，请除以 $\\operatorname{med}(b)$。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:475
msgid "The bootstrap assumes exchangeable deltas. Rotation order makes neighbouring blocks dependent; the interval does not model that."
msgstr "自助法假设差值是可交换的。轮换顺序使相邻区组相互依赖；区间并未对此建模。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:477
msgid "`filter_outliers` is never applied automatically, and `OutlierPolicy` in a `RunProtocol` is a recorded intent, not an action."
msgstr "`filter_outliers` 从不自动应用，`RunProtocol` 中的 `OutlierPolicy` 是记录下来的意图，而不是一个动作。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:479
msgid "Non-finite values are rejected with an error only by the bootstrap functions; `summarize` and `compare_paired` propagate `NaN` as derived above."
msgstr "只有自助法函数会用错误拒绝非有限值；`summarize` 和 `compare_paired` 按上文推导的方式传播 `NaN`。"

#: manual/design/stats.md:482
msgid "The bootstrap interval has no coverage guarantee for small $n$ (see the coverage table). An interval with guaranteed coverage for the median is the order-statistic interval $[d_{(i)}, d_{(j)}]$ with $i$ and $j$ chosen from $\\mathrm{Bin}(n, \\tfrac12)$; it is not provided."
msgstr "自助法区间在小 $n$ 时没有覆盖率保证（见覆盖率表）。对中位数有覆盖率保证的区间是次序统计量区间 $[d_{(i)}, d_{(j)}]$，其中 $i$ 和 $j$ 由 $\\mathrm{Bin}(n, \\tfrac12)$ 选定；本包不提供它。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:1
msgid "tune design"
msgstr "tune 设计"

#: manual/design/tune.md:5
msgid "Auto-tuning picks a configuration (block sizes, kernel variant, layout) by measuring candidates. Done naively it overfits: the \"winner\" is often the candidate whose noise happened to be favourable, on the shapes that happened to be measured. `tune` provides the policy pieces that prevent this, robust scores, practical ties, confirmation and holdouts, while leaving the building and running of candidates to the application, where they can be validated and measured like any other benchmark."
msgstr "自动调优通过测量候选来选择配置（块大小、内核变体、布局）。若做得天真，它会过拟合：所谓“胜者”往往只是在恰好被测量的形状上、噪声恰好有利的那个候选。`tune` 提供防止这种情况的策略组件——稳健分数、实际意义上的持平、确认和留出集——同时把候选的构建和运行留给应用，在那里它们可以像其他任何基准测试一样被验证和测量。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:15
msgid "Candidates must be validated and measured like any other benchmark, so the package cannot run them itself."
msgstr "候选必须像任何其他基准测试一样被验证和测量，因此该包不能自己运行它们。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:17
msgid "Tuning measurements are noisy and the candidate spaces are large."
msgstr "调优测量有噪声，候选空间很大。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:18
msgid "The policy must be testable with made-up numbers and reproducible from a seed."
msgstr "策略必须能用编造的数字来测试，并能从种子复现。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:25
msgid "A candidate $c$ measured $n$ times has samples $t_1, \\dots, t_n$. Its score is the median of the usable samples (finite, non-negative), for the robustness reasons derived in the [stats design](stats.md). A secondary metric $s_c$ (workspace bytes, code size) breaks ties."
msgstr "一个被测量 $n$ 次的候选 $c$ 具有样本 $t_1, \\dots, t_n$。基于 [stats 设计](stats.md)中推导的稳健性理由，它的分数是可用样本（有限、非负）的中位数。次要指标 $s_c$（工作区字节数、代码大小）用于决出持平。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:30
msgid "The winner's curse"
msgstr "赢家诅咒"

#: manual/design/tune.md:32
msgid "Let $\\hat p_c = p_c + \\varepsilon_c$ be the measured score of candidate $c$ with true cost $p_c$ and zero-mean noise. Choosing the minimum of the measurements is biased downward:"
msgstr "设 $\\hat p_c = p_c + \\varepsilon_c$ 为候选 $c$ 的测量分数，其真实代价为 $p_c$，噪声均值为零。选取测量值的最小值是向下有偏的："

#: manual/design/tune.md:40
msgid "because $\\min_c \\hat p_c \\le \\hat p_{c^*}$ for the truly best $c^*$, and taking expectations gives $\\mathbb E[\\min_c \\hat p_c] \\le p_{c^*}$. With many candidates of similar cost, the selected one is more likely to be lucky than good. Two remedies follow, and `TuningBudget` names both: re-measure the `finalists` with fresh `confirmation_samples` (the new noise is independent of the selection, so the confirmed score is unbiased), and evaluate the winner on a `holdout` it was not selected on."
msgstr "因为对真正最好的 $c^*$ 有 $\\min_c \\hat p_c \\le \\hat p_{c^*}$，取期望得到 $\\mathbb E[\\min_c \\hat p_c] \\le p_{c^*}$。当有许多代价相近的候选时，被选中的那个更可能是运气好而不是真的好。由此得到两种补救措施，`TuningBudget` 为两者都命了名：用新的 `confirmation_samples` 重新测量 `finalists`（新的噪声与选择无关，因此确认后的分数是无偏的），以及在胜者未参与选择的 `holdout` 上评估它。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:48
msgid "Practical ties"
msgstr "实际意义上的持平"

#: manual/design/tune.md:50
msgid "`select_best` with threshold $t$ forms the tie set"
msgstr "阈值为 $t$ 的 `select_best` 构成持平集"

#: manual/design/tune.md:56
msgid "(for $p_{\\min} = 0$, $F = \\{\\, c : p_c = 0 \\,\\}$; a threshold that is `NaN`, infinite or negative counts as $t = 0$), and returns the element of $F$ with the best secondary value, then the smallest id. Ids are compared with MoonBit's `String` order, which compares lengths first and then code units, so `\"b\"` precedes `\"aa\"`. The rule is order independent: $F$ is defined by values only, and the second step is the minimum of a total order (secondary, then id) on $F$, which is unique when ids are unique. So permuting the input cannot change the result."
msgstr "（当 $p_{\\min} = 0$ 时，$F = \\{\\, c : p_c = 0 \\,\\}$；`NaN`、无穷大或负的阈值按 $t = 0$ 计），并返回 $F$ 中次要值最好的元素，再按最小 id 决出。id 用 MoonBit 的 `String` 顺序比较，它先比较长度、再比较代码单元，因此 `\"b\"` 排在 `\"aa\"` 之前。该规则与顺序无关：$F$ 只由值定义，而第二步是 $F$ 上一个全序（先次要值、再 id）的最小值，当 id 唯一时它是唯一的。因此对输入进行置换不会改变结果。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:65
msgid "Pareto dominance"
msgstr "Pareto 支配"

#: manual/design/tune.md:67
msgid ""
"With both metrics minimized, $o$ dominates $c$ ($o \\prec c$) when $p_o \\le p_c$, $s_o \\le s_c$ and $(p_o, s_o) \\n"
"e (p_c, s_c)$. The frontier is $\\{c : \\n"
"exists\\, o \\prec c\\}$. Sorted by primary cost, the frontier has strictly decreasing secondary cost: if $p_a < p_b$ and $s_a \\le s_b$ then $a \\prec b$, a contradiction, so $s_a > s_b$. Points with equal primary cost on the frontier must also have equal secondary cost. Every point off the frontier is dominated by a point on it (dominance is a strict partial order on a finite set, so every chain ends in a minimal element)."
msgstr ""
"在两个指标都取最小化时，若 $p_o \\le p_c$、$s_o \\le s_c$ 且 $(p_o, s_o) \\n"
"e (p_c, s_c)$，则 $o$ 支配 $c$（$o \\prec c$）。前沿为 $\\{c : \\n"
"exists\\, o \\prec c\\}$。按主要代价排序时，前沿上的次要代价严格递减：若 $p_a < p_b$ 且 $s_a \\le s_b$，则 $a \\prec b$，矛盾，因此 $s_a > s_b$。前沿上主要代价相等的点，其次要代价也必须相等。前沿之外的每个点都被前沿上的某个点支配（支配是有限集上的严格偏序，因此每条链都终止于一个极小元）。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:76
msgid "Random subsets of a large space"
msgstr "大空间的随机子集"

#: manual/design/tune.md:78
msgid "Take the first $B$ of $N$ candidates in a uniformly random order, and let a fraction $q$ of the space be \"good\". The prefix misses every good candidate with probability"
msgstr "按均匀随机顺序取 $N$ 个候选中的前 $B$ 个，并设空间中比例为 $q$ 的部分是“好的”。前缀错过所有好候选的概率为"

#: manual/design/tune.md:88
msgid "because each factor is at most $1 - q$. So the prefix contains at least one good candidate with probability at least $1 - (1 - q)^{B}$, whatever $N$ is. $B = 60$ already gives $1 - 0.95^{60} \\approx 0.954$ for the top 5 %. This is the classical argument for random search over grids.[^random]"
msgstr "因为每个因子至多为 $1 - q$。因此无论 $N$ 是多少，前缀至少包含一个好候选的概率至少为 $1 - (1 - q)^{B}$。$B = 60$ 时，对前 5 % 就已经有 $1 - 0.95^{60} \\approx 0.954$。这是支持随机搜索优于网格搜索的经典论证。[^random]"

#: manual/design/tune.md:93
msgid "`seeded_order` approximates such an order by sorting candidates on a seeded key $k = \\mathrm{mix}(h)$, where $h$ is the 64-bit FNV-1a hash of the id with the seed folded into the offset basis and $\\mathrm{mix}$ is the SplitMix64 output finalizer"
msgstr "`seeded_order` 通过按带种子的键 $k = \\mathrm{mix}(h)$ 对候选排序来近似这样的顺序，其中 $h$ 是把种子并入偏移基数后 id 的 64 位 FNV-1a 哈希，$\\mathrm{mix}$ 是 SplitMix64 输出终结器"

#: manual/design/tune.md:106
msgid "The argument needs the key order to behave like a random permutation, and FNV-1a alone does so only partly. The last character $c$ of an id enters as $h' = (h \\oplus c)\\cdot(2^{40} + 435)$: it changes the low byte of $h \\oplus c$, which the factor $2^{40}$ moves to bits 40–47, and reaches the top bits, which decide the sort, only through carries. Sorting on $h$ itself kept ids that differ only in their last characters next to each other (for `\"c0\"` to `\"c99\"` and seed `1`, the first ten were `c0` to `c9`).[^issue10] Each step of $\\mathrm{mix}$ is a bijection (an xorshift and a multiplication by an odd constant), so distinct hashes keep distinct keys, and the right shifts feed the high bits back into the low ones before each multiplication carries them up again: one changed input bit changes each output bit with probability close to $1/2$. The key order is then a pseudo-random permutation for every pattern of ids."
msgstr "该论证要求键的顺序表现得像随机置换，而单靠 FNV-1a 只能部分做到。id 的最后一个字符 $c$ 以 $h' = (h \\oplus c)\\cdot(2^{40} + 435)$ 的形式进入：它改变 $h \\oplus c$ 的低字节，因子 $2^{40}$ 把这个字节移到第 40–47 位，而它只能通过进位到达决定排序的高位。直接按 $h$ 排序会让只在最后几个字符上不同的 id 彼此相邻（对于 `\"c0\"` 到 `\"c99\"` 和种子 `1`，前十个曾是 `c0` 到 `c9`）。[^issue10] $\\mathrm{mix}$ 的每一步都是双射（一次 xorshift 和一次乘以奇数常数），因此不同的哈希得到不同的键；右移在每次乘法把低位进位到高位之前，先把高位反馈到低位：改变一个输入位会以接近 $1/2$ 的概率改变每个输出位。于是，对任何形式的 id，键的顺序都是一个伪随机置换。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:120
msgid "[Issue #10](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mare_mark/issues/10). Adding the finalizer changed the order for every seed."
msgstr "[Issue #10](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/mare_mark/issues/10)。加入终结器改变了每个种子对应的顺序。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:122
msgid "J. Bergstra and Y. Bengio, \"Random search for hyper-parameter optimization\", *JMLR* 13, 2012."
msgstr "J. Bergstra 和 Y. Bengio，\"Random search for hyper-parameter optimization\"，*JMLR* 13，2012。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:126
msgid "Policy here, effects in the application"
msgstr "策略在此，副作用在应用中"

#: manual/design/tune.md:128
msgid "*Problem.* Building a candidate may mean compiling a kernel; running it must be validated and timed under a protocol. *Choice.* `tune` takes scores as input and never runs anything; `BuiltCandidate` carries a `runner.Implementation`. *Why.* Tuning measurements then go through the same validation, calibration and event stream as every other benchmark, and the tuning policy is testable with made-up numbers."
msgstr "*问题。* 构建候选可能意味着编译一个内核；运行它则必须在某个协议下经过验证和计时。*选择。* `tune` 以分数作为输入，从不运行任何东西；`BuiltCandidate` 携带一个 `runner.Implementation`。*理由。* 这样调优测量就与其他所有基准测试一样经过相同的验证、校准和事件流，而调优策略可以用编造的数字来测试。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:135
msgid "Median scores"
msgstr "中位数分数"

#: manual/design/tune.md:137
msgid "`score_samples` takes the median of usable samples and marks a candidate with no usable sample invalid, so a candidate cannot win because a broken measurement returned `0` or `NaN`."
msgstr "`score_samples` 取可用样本的中位数，并把没有可用样本的候选标记为无效，因此候选不会因为某次出错的测量返回 `0` 或 `NaN` 而胜出。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:141
msgid "Exhaustive search over a bounded prefix"
msgstr "在有界前缀上穷举搜索"

#: manual/design/tune.md:143
msgid "`exhaustive_scores` scores the first `budget` candidates of the enumeration and records a `BuildEvent` for each, including rejected ones. Combined with `seeded_order`, the prefix is a reproducible subset (random to the extent discussed above); with the natural order and a large budget, it is a full grid search. The policy string `global:<id>` names the candidate with the smallest measured primary score, the first one on ties. That is the raw minimum, which the winner's curse argument above warns against: treat it as a shortlist entry, not a decision. Decisions (with practical ties, per shape, Pareto) are built with `select_best`, `pareto_frontier` and `@model.DeploymentPolicy`."
msgstr "`exhaustive_scores` 为枚举中的前 `budget` 个候选打分，并为每个候选（包括被拒绝的）记录一个 `BuildEvent`。与 `seeded_order` 结合时，前缀是一个可复现的子集（其随机程度如上所述）；采用自然顺序和较大的预算时，它就是完整的网格搜索。策略字符串 `global:<id>` 指明测得主要分数最小的候选，持平时取第一个。这就是原始最小值，也正是上面赢家诅咒论证所警告的：请把它当作候选名单中的一项，而不是决策。决策（带实际持平、按形状、Pareto）用 `select_best`、`pareto_frontier` 和 `@model.DeploymentPolicy` 构建。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:153
msgid "Adaptive confirmation"
msgstr "自适应确认"

#: manual/design/tune.md:155
msgid "`confirmation_count` multiplies the base confirmation count by 1, 2 or 3 as the relative uncertainty crosses 5 % and 20 %, clamped to the budget. Noisy finalists get more samples, quiet ones do not waste time."
msgstr "`confirmation_count` 在相对不确定度越过 5 % 和 20 % 时，把基础确认次数乘以 1、2 或 3，并截断到预算之内。噪声大的决赛候选获得更多样本，安静的候选则不浪费时间。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:161
msgid "`select_best` returns `None` exactly when no score is usable; otherwise its result is usable, within the threshold of the fastest, and independent of input order (derived above)."
msgstr "`select_best` 恰好在没有可用分数时返回 `None`；否则其结果是可用的、在最快者的阈值范围内，并且与输入顺序无关（推导见上文）。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:164
msgid "`pareto_frontier` returns only usable, non-dominated scores, sorted by primary, secondary, id."
msgstr "`pareto_frontier` 只返回可用且非支配的分数，按主要值、次要值、id 排序。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:166
msgid "`exhaustive_scores` examines at most `budget` candidates and calls the score callback only for valid ones."
msgstr "`exhaustive_scores` 最多检查 `budget` 个候选，并且只对有效候选调用打分回调。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:168
msgid "`seeded_order` is a permutation of its input that depends only on the ids and the seed."
msgstr "`seeded_order` 是其输入的一个置换，只取决于 id 和种子。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:170
msgid "`confirmation_count` lies in $[0, \\max(\\text{budget}, 0)]$."
msgstr "`confirmation_count` 位于 $[0, \\max(\\text{budget}, 0)]$ 中。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:174
msgid "**Bayesian optimization or evolutionary search.** Effective, but needs a model of the space and makes results harder to reproduce; the hooks (`neighbors`, `seeded_order`) allow a user-written search."
msgstr "**贝叶斯优化或进化搜索。** 有效，但需要对空间建模，并使结果更难复现；钩子（`neighbors`、`seeded_order`）允许用户自行编写搜索。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:177
msgid "**Mean scores.** One preempted run would decide."
msgstr "**均值分数。** 一次被抢占的运行就会左右结果。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:178
msgid "**Selecting the raw minimum.** Subject to the winner's curse. Only the informational policy string of `exhaustive_scores` uses it."
msgstr "**选取原始最小值。** 会受到赢家诅咒的影响。只有 `exhaustive_scores` 的信息性策略字符串使用它。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:183
msgid "No candidate is built, run or validated here."
msgstr "这里不构建、运行或验证任何候选。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:184
msgid "`TuningBudget`, `TuningObjective` and `HoldoutPlan` are data; no function enforces them."
msgstr "`TuningBudget`、`TuningObjective` 和 `HoldoutPlan` 是数据；没有函数强制执行它们。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:186
msgid "`CandidateSpace.neighbors` is not used by any function in the package."
msgstr "本包中没有任何函数使用 `CandidateSpace.neighbors`。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:187
msgid "`exhaustive_scores` does not use `seeded_order` itself; reorder the space first if you want a random subset."
msgstr "`exhaustive_scores` 本身不使用 `seeded_order`；如果你想要随机子集，请先对空间重新排序。"

#: manual/design/tune.md:189
msgid "`seeded_order` is pseudo-random, not cryptographic: the order is a fixed function of the ids and the seed."
msgstr "`seeded_order` 是伪随机的，而不是密码学意义上的：顺序是 id 和种子的固定函数。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:1
msgid "tune_gemm design"
msgstr "tune_gemm 设计"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:5
msgid "`tune_gemm` is the reference domain for `tune`: a problem where blocking parameters matter, correctness can be checked exactly, and every candidate can be serialized. It shows the full tuning discipline (validate before timing, account for workspace, test tails, record the configuration and the environment) on matrix multiplication, without depending on hardware-specific kernels."
msgstr "`tune_gemm` 是 `tune` 的参考领域：一个分块参数很重要、正确性可以精确检查、且每个候选都可以序列化的问题。它在矩阵乘法上展示了完整的调优规范（先验证再计时、统计工作区、测试尾部、记录配置和环境），而不依赖于特定硬件的内核。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:14
msgid "The kernels must run on every MoonBit backend, so they use scalar code only."
msgstr "内核必须能在每个 MoonBit 后端上运行，因此只使用标量代码。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:16
msgid "The built-in kernel must be checkable against the reference with tolerance `0`."
msgstr "内置内核必须能以容差 `0` 与参考实现对照检查。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:18
msgid "Inputs must be reproducible from a seed on every target."
msgstr "输入必须能在每个目标上从种子复现。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:22
msgid "The product and its layouts"
msgstr "乘积及其布局"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:24
msgid "For each batch $b$, $C_b = A_b B_b$ with $c_{ij} = \\sum_{l=0}^{k-1} a_{il}\\, b_{lj}$, which costs $2mnk$ floating-point operations. A measured time of $t$ µs per operation therefore corresponds to"
msgstr "对每个批次 $b$，$C_b = A_b B_b$，其中 $c_{ij} = \\sum_{l=0}^{k-1} a_{il}\\, b_{lj}$，代价为 $2mnk$ 次浮点运算。因此每次操作 $t$ µs 的测量时间对应于"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:32
msgid "An $r \\times c$ matrix stores element $(i, j)$ of batch $b$ at $b\\,rc + i\\,c + j$ in row-major and $b\\,rc + j\\,r + i$ in column-major layout; both maps are bijections from index triples onto $[0, \\text{batch}\\cdot rc)$, so every layout combination describes the same mathematical product."
msgstr "一个 $r \\times c$ 矩阵把第 $b$ 个批次的元素 $(i, j)$ 存放在 $b\\,rc + i\\,c + j$（行主序布局）或 $b\\,rc + j\\,r + i$（列主序布局）；这两个映射都是从索引三元组到 $[0, \\text{batch}\\cdot rc)$ 的双射，因此每种布局组合描述的都是同一个数学乘积。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:37
msgid "Blocking and workspace"
msgstr "分块与工作区"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:39
msgid "`gemm_blocked` partitions the iteration space into $mc \\times nc \\times kc$ blocks and each block into $mr \\times nr$ register tiles. One block touches an $mc \\times kc$ block of $A$, a $kc \\times nc$ panel of $B$ and an $mc \\times nc$ block of $C$:"
msgstr "`gemm_blocked` 把迭代空间划分为 $mc \\times nc \\times kc$ 块，再把每个块划分为 $mr \\times nr$ 寄存器分片。一个块涉及 $A$ 的一个 $mc \\times kc$ 块、$B$ 的一个 $kc \\times nc$ 面板和 $C$ 的一个 $mc \\times nc$ 块："

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:50
msgid "For a cube $mc = nc = kc = s$, $W = 24 s^2$ and $I = s/12$: larger blocks reuse each loaded value more often, until $W$ exceeds the cache that should hold it. That trade-off is what tuning searches, and `workspace_bytes` is $W$, used by `valid_candidate` as a hard limit. The largest default candidate, $128 \\times 128 \\times 64$, needs $W = 8(8192 + 8192 + 16384) = 262144$ bytes.[^goto]"
msgstr "对于立方体 $mc = nc = kc = s$，$W = 24 s^2$ 且 $I = s/12$：块越大，每个加载的值被复用得越频繁，直到 $W$ 超出本应容纳它的缓存。调优搜索的正是这种权衡，而 `workspace_bytes` 就是 $W$，被 `valid_candidate` 用作硬性上限。默认候选中最大的 $128 \\times 128 \\times 64$ 需要 $W = 8(8192 + 8192 + 16384) = 262144$ 字节。[^goto]"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:56
msgid "K. Goto and R. A. van de Geijn, \"Anatomy of high-performance matrix multiplication\", *ACM TOMS* 34(3), 2008."
msgstr "K. Goto 和 R. A. van de Geijn，\"Anatomy of high-performance matrix multiplication\"，*ACM TOMS* 34(3)，2008。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:58
msgid "Exactness of the blocked kernel"
msgstr "分块内核的精确性"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:60
msgid "For every entry, `gemm_reference` computes"
msgstr "对每个元素，`gemm_reference` 计算"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:66
msgid "`gemm_blocked` starts each entry at $0.0$ in the first $k$ block, stores the partial sum in $C$ (a double, so storing is exact), reloads it in the next $k$ block and continues in increasing $l$. It performs the same operations on the same operands in the same order, so the two results are bitwise identical as long as the compiler treats both loops alike (in particular, does not contract one of them into fused multiply-adds). Packing only copies values. The correctness check can therefore use tolerance $0$ for the built-in kernel."
msgstr "`gemm_blocked` 在第一个 $k$ 块中从 $0.0$ 开始计算每个元素，把部分和存入 $C$（双精度数，因此存储是精确的），在下一个 $k$ 块中重新加载并按 $l$ 递增的顺序继续。它以相同的顺序对相同的操作数执行相同的运算，因此只要编译器对两个循环一视同仁（特别是不把其中之一收缩为融合乘加），两个结果就逐位相同。打包只是复制值。因此对内置内核，正确性检查可以使用容差 $0$。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:74
msgid "A kernel that reorders the summation (a vectorized microkernel, a different loop order) is only close. With unit roundoff $u = 2^{-53}$ and $\\gamma_k = ku/(1 - ku)$, any order of summation satisfies[^higham]"
msgstr "对求和重新排序的内核（向量化的微内核、不同的循环顺序）只能做到接近。设单位舍入误差 $u = 2^{-53}$、$\\gamma_k = ku/(1 - ku)$，任何求和顺序都满足[^higham]"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:82
msgid "so two such kernels differ by at most $2\\gamma_k \\sum_l \\lvert a_{il}\\rvert\\lvert b_{lj}\\rvert$. With entries from `reproducible_matrix`, $\\lvert a\\rvert, \\lvert b\\rvert \\le 1$ and the bound is $2\\gamma_k k \\approx 2k^2 u$: for $k = 64$, about $9.1\\cdot 10^{-13}$. That is the absolute tolerance to pass to `validate_gemm` for a reordering kernel on these inputs."
msgstr "因此两个这样的内核至多相差 $2\\gamma_k \\sum_l \\lvert a_{il}\\rvert\\lvert b_{lj}\\rvert$。对于来自 `reproducible_matrix` 的元素，$\\lvert a\\rvert, \\lvert b\\rvert \\le 1$，界为 $2\\gamma_k k \\approx 2k^2 u$：当 $k = 64$ 时约为 $9.1\\cdot 10^{-13}$。这就是在这些输入上为重排序内核传给 `validate_gemm` 的绝对容差。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:88
msgid "N. J. Higham, *Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*, 2nd ed., SIAM, 2002, §3.1."
msgstr "N. J. Higham，*Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms*，第 2 版，SIAM，2002，§3.1。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:90
msgid "Reproducible inputs"
msgstr "可复现的输入"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:92
msgid "`reproducible_matrix(seed, r, c, layout)` runs the 64-bit linear congruential generator"
msgstr "`reproducible_matrix(seed, r, c, layout)` 运行 64 位线性同余生成器"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:99
msgid "and maps each state $x_1, x_2, \\dots$ (the state is advanced before the first value is drawn) to $v = \\bigl((x \\gg 32) \\bmod 2001\\bigr)/1000 - 1$. The multiplier is $\\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$ and the increment is odd, so by the Hull–Dobell theorem the generator has the full period $2^{64}$. The 32-bit value $x \\gg 32$ is reduced modulo 2001: since $2^{32} = 2146410 \\cdot 2001 + 886$, 886 of the 2001 values are slightly more likely, by a relative $1/2146410 \\approx 4.7\\cdot 10^{-7}$. Entries are $j/1000 - 1$ for $j \\in \\{0, \\dots, 2000\\}$, evaluated in double precision, so they lie in $[-1, 1]$ and are multiples of $0.001$ up to rounding. The logical matrix is generated in row-major order and then stored in the requested layout, so the layout does not change the values."
msgstr "并把每个状态 $x_1, x_2, \\dots$（在抽取第一个值之前状态先前进一步）映射为 $v = \\bigl((x \\gg 32) \\bmod 2001\\bigr)/1000 - 1$。乘数满足 $\\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$ 且增量为奇数，因此由 Hull–Dobell 定理，该生成器具有满周期 $2^{64}$。32 位值 $x \\gg 32$ 对 2001 取模：由于 $2^{32} = 2146410 \\cdot 2001 + 886$，2001 个值中有 886 个出现的可能性略高，相对高出 $1/2146410 \\approx 4.7\\cdot 10^{-7}$。元素为 $j/1000 - 1$（$j \\in \\{0, \\dots, 2000\\}$），以双精度求值，因此它们位于 $[-1, 1]$ 中，并在舍入意义下是 $0.001$ 的倍数。逻辑矩阵按行主序生成，然后以请求的布局存储，因此布局不会改变值。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:110
msgid "Tails"
msgstr "尾部"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:112
msgid "Edge tiles handle $m$, $n$ or $k$ that are not multiples of the block sizes. `boundary_shapes` returns $m - 1$, $m$ and $m + 1$: for $m$ a multiple of $mr$, these exercise a short tile, an exact fit and a one-row tail."
msgstr "边缘分片处理不是块大小倍数的 $m$、$n$ 或 $k$。`boundary_shapes` 返回 $m - 1$、$m$ 和 $m + 1$：当 $m$ 是 $mr$ 的倍数时，它们分别考验短分片、恰好整除和单行尾部。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:118
msgid "A portable scalar kernel"
msgstr "可移植的标量内核"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:120
msgid "*Problem.* Real GEMM tuning depends on SIMD microkernels that differ per target. *Choice.* One scalar blocked kernel, with `microkernel_id` as a label. *Why.* The package demonstrates and tests the tuning machinery on every backend; a harness can map the label to its own kernels."
msgstr "*问题。* 真实的 GEMM 调优依赖于因目标而异的 SIMD 微内核。*选择。* 一个标量分块内核，以 `microkernel_id` 作为标签。*理由。* 该包在每个后端上演示并测试调优机制；测试框架可以把该标签映射到自己的内核。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:125
msgid "Validate before measuring"
msgstr "先验证再测量"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:127
msgid "`gemm_is_correct` runs the candidate and compares with the reference before the candidate is ever timed. `execute_candidate` returns `None` for invalid candidates or shapes instead of a result that would look like a fast, empty multiplication."
msgstr "`gemm_is_correct` 在候选被计时之前就运行它并与参考比较。对于无效的候选或形状，`execute_candidate` 返回 `None`，而不是返回一个看起来像快速空乘法的结果。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:132
msgid "Workspace as a hard constraint"
msgstr "工作区作为硬约束"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:134
msgid "The memory a candidate needs is computed from its parameters and checked against a limit before execution, so the search never selects a configuration that cannot run in the target's memory budget."
msgstr "候选所需的内存由其参数算出，并在执行前与上限比较，因此搜索永远不会选中一个无法在目标内存预算内运行的配置。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:138
msgid "Explicit timing scope"
msgstr "显式的计时范围"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:140
msgid "`TimingScope` and `AllocationMode` are part of the candidate and of its id, so \"compute only\" and \"end to end\" results are never compared as if they measured the same thing."
msgstr "`TimingScope` 和 `AllocationMode` 是候选及其 id 的一部分，因此“仅计算”和“端到端”的结果永远不会被当作测量同一事物来比较。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:144
msgid "Serialized configurations"
msgstr "序列化的配置"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:146
msgid "`config_json` writes everything needed to repeat a tuning run, with 64-bit values as strings and a schema version `mmkts_1`. Together with a `GemmEnvironment` it says where a tuned result is valid."
msgstr "`config_json` 写出重复一次调优运行所需的一切，64 位值写为字符串，模式版本为 `mmkts_1`。它与 `GemmEnvironment` 一起说明调优结果在何处有效。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:152
msgid "`gemm_blocked` equals `gemm_reference` bit for bit under the condition above; the tests check all eight layout combinations with tails."
msgstr "在上述条件下，`gemm_blocked` 与 `gemm_reference` 逐位相等；测试检查了带尾部的全部八种布局组合。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:154
msgid "`workspace_bytes(c) <= limit` for every valid candidate."
msgstr "对每个有效候选都有 `workspace_bytes(c) <= limit`。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:155
msgid "`enumerate_gemm_candidates` returns the same 486 candidates in the same order, all valid for the limit 262144."
msgstr "`enumerate_gemm_candidates` 以相同的顺序返回相同的 486 个候选，它们在上限 262144 下全部有效。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:157
msgid "`reproducible_matrix` depends only on its arguments; the row-major and column-major results describe the same logical matrix."
msgstr "`reproducible_matrix` 只取决于其参数；行主序和列主序的结果描述同一个逻辑矩阵。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:159
msgid "`validate_gemm` counts every element of a length difference as a mismatch, so truncated results are never valid."
msgstr "`validate_gemm` 把长度差异中的每个元素都计为不匹配，因此被截断的结果永远不会有效。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:164
msgid "**Target-specific microkernels.** Not portable across MoonBit backends."
msgstr "**针对特定目标的微内核。** 无法在 MoonBit 后端之间移植。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:165
msgid "**Relative tolerances in validation.** Entries of $C$ can be near zero; the absolute bound above is the honest one for bounded inputs."
msgstr "**验证中使用相对容差。** $C$ 的元素可能接近零；对有界输入而言，上面的绝对界才是诚实的界。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:167
msgid "**Generating inputs with the platform random generator.** Not reproducible across targets."
msgstr "**用平台随机生成器生成输入。** 无法跨目标复现。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:172
msgid "Only `m_n_k` loop order and scalar code; the three microkernel ids run the same loop."
msgstr "只有 `m_n_k` 循环顺序和标量代码；三个微内核 id 运行同一个循环。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:174
msgid "`pack_operand` copies a whole operand into row-major order; it does not build cache-sized packed panels."
msgstr "`pack_operand` 把整个操作数复制为行主序；它不构建缓存大小的打包面板。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:176
msgid "`allocation_mode`, `timing_scope` and `reuse_count` are descriptive: the kernel allocates its result on every call; the harness decides what to time."
msgstr "`allocation_mode`、`timing_scope` 和 `reuse_count` 是描述性的：内核在每次调用时都分配其结果；计时什么由测试框架决定。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:178
msgid "No search loop: `tune` and the application drive the search."
msgstr "没有搜索循环：由 `tune` 和应用驱动搜索。"

#: manual/design/tune_gemm.md:179
msgid "`reproducible_matrix` makes one matrix; batched operands are concatenated by the caller."
msgstr "`reproducible_matrix` 生成一个矩阵；批量操作数由调用者拼接。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:1
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "快速入门"

#: manual/getting_started.md:3
msgid "This guide takes you from an empty package to a validated benchmark, a statistical decision and an HTML report in one test. It then shows the command-line tools on the fixtures shipped with the repository."
msgstr "本指南在一个测试中带你从一个空包走到经过验证的基准测试、统计决策和 HTML 报告。随后它会在仓库附带的测试数据上展示命令行工具。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:7
msgid "1. Add the module"
msgstr "1. 添加模块"

#: manual/getting_started.md:9
msgid "You need MoonBit with `moonc` 0.10 or later."
msgstr "你需要 `moonc` 0.10 或更高版本的 MoonBit。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:15
msgid "In the `moon.pkg` of the package that holds your benchmarks:"
msgstr "在存放基准测试的包的 `moon.pkg` 中："

#: manual/getting_started.md:28
msgid "2. Benchmark, decide, report"
msgstr "2. 基准测试、决策、报告"

#: manual/getting_started.md:30
msgid "The test below compares two ways to compute the sum of squares $0^2 + 1^2 + \\dots + (n-1)^2$: a loop and the closed form $(n-1)n(2n-1)/6$."
msgstr "下面的测试比较两种计算平方和 $0^2 + 1^2 + \\dots + (n-1)^2$ 的方法：循环和闭式公式 $(n-1)n(2n-1)/6$。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:98
msgid "What happened:"
msgstr "发生了什么："

#: manual/getting_started.md:100
msgid "`against_equal` attached the loop as the reference oracle. Both implementations were validated on both scales before any timing (four passed validations)."
msgstr "`against_equal` 把循环作为参考判定器附加上去。在任何计时之前，两个实现都在两个规模上经过了验证（四次验证通过）。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:103
msgid "`Development` warmed every implementation up, calibrated a batch size per implementation, then ran 3 exploratory and 10 confirmatory blocks per scale, rotating the order of the two implementations."
msgstr "`Development` 对每个实现进行预热，为每个实现校准批次大小，然后在每个规模上运行 3 个探索性区组和 10 个验证性区组，并轮换两个实现的顺序。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:106
msgid "The confirmatory blocks are paired by position (block $i$ of the loop with block $i$ of the formula). `comparison.decision` and `comparison.speedup` depend on your machine; the formula is expected to be `Faster`."
msgstr "验证性区组按位置配对（循环的第 $i$ 个区组与公式的第 $i$ 个区组）。`comparison.decision` 和 `comparison.speedup` 取决于你的机器；预期公式为 `Faster`。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:110
msgid "The JSONL record (`record.to_jsonl()`) holds every event; save it next to the HTML."
msgstr "JSONL 记录（`record.to_jsonl()`）保存了每个事件；请把它保存在 HTML 旁边。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:113
msgid "Run it with `moon test --target native`. The test also runs on `js` and `wasm`."
msgstr "用 `moon test --target native` 运行它。该测试也可以在 `js` 和 `wasm` 上运行。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:116
msgid "3. Use the command line"
msgstr "3. 使用命令行"

#: manual/getting_started.md:118
msgid "From a checkout of the repository:"
msgstr "在仓库的检出目录中："

#: manual/getting_started.md:126
msgid "`report` writes a self-contained HTML file. `replay --dry-run` prints the command recorded in a validation failure; add `--yes` instead of `--dry-run` to execute it. See the [cli tutorial](tutorial/cli.md)."
msgstr "`report` 写出一个自包含的 HTML 文件。`replay --dry-run` 打印验证失败中记录的命令；把 `--dry-run` 换成 `--yes` 即可执行它。参见 [cli 教程](tutorial/cli.md)。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:130
msgid "Common first mistakes"
msgstr "常见的入门错误"

#: manual/getting_started.md:132
msgid "Doing setup work (allocation, parsing, copying) inside the implementation function, where it is timed. Put it in a fixture."
msgstr "在实现函数内部做准备工作（分配、解析、复制），使其被计时。请把它放到夹具中。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:134
msgid "Comparing arrays from different blocks, phases, datasets or targets."
msgstr "比较来自不同区组、阶段、数据集或目标的数组。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:135
msgid "Treating `Unsupported`, a timeout or a validation failure as a number."
msgstr "把 `Unsupported`、超时或验证失败当作数字。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:136
msgid "Executing a replay artifact without reading it with `--dry-run` first."
msgstr "未先用 `--dry-run` 阅读就执行重放产物。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:137
msgid "Reusing `summary.run_id` as a unique id; it names the protocol and the case."
msgstr "把 `summary.run_id` 当作唯一 id 复用；它指明的是协议和用例。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:139
msgid "Where to go next"
msgstr "下一步"

#: manual/getting_started.md:141
msgid "[runner tutorial](tutorial/runner.md) for fixtures, sequences, shrinking and protocols."
msgstr "[runner 教程](tutorial/runner.md)：夹具、序列、缩减和协议。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:143
msgid "[stats tutorial](tutorial/stats.md) for decisions and intervals."
msgstr "[stats 教程](tutorial/stats.md)：决策和区间。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:144
msgid "[architecture](architecture.md) for how the packages fit together."
msgstr "[架构](architecture.md)：各个包如何组合在一起。"

#: manual/index.md:1
msgid "mare_mark"
msgstr "mare_mark"

#: manual/index.md:3
msgid "This manual documents the `0.3.0` release of `Luna-Flow/mare_mark`."
msgstr "本手册记录 `Luna-Flow/mare_mark` 的 `0.3.0` 版本。"

#: manual/index.md:5
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概述"

#: manual/index.md:7
msgid "`mare_mark` is a benchmarking harness for MoonBit. It validates every implementation against an oracle before timing it, measures in calibrated batches and balanced blocks, keeps every raw observation in an append-only JSONL record, compares implementations with robust, paired statistics and a seeded bootstrap, supports auto-tuning with practical ties and Pareto fronts, and renders self-contained HTML reports. The `pkg.generated.mbti` file of each package is the authority for its public names and signatures."
msgstr "`mare_mark` 是一个面向 MoonBit 的基准测试框架。它在计时之前用判定器验证每个实现，以校准过的批次和平衡区组进行测量，把每个原始观测保存在只追加的 JSONL 记录中，用稳健的成对统计和带种子的自助法比较实现，支持带实际持平和 Pareto 前沿的自动调优，并渲染自包含的 HTML 报告。每个包的 `pkg.generated.mbti` 文件是其公开名称和签名的权威来源。"

#: manual/index.md:15
msgid "The release centers on four ideas:"
msgstr "本版本围绕四个理念："

#: manual/index.md:17
msgid "A fast wrong answer never looks like a speedup: validation precedes timing, and a failing implementation is removed from the plots."
msgstr "快速但错误的答案永远不会看起来像加速：验证先于计时，失败的实现会从图表中移除。"

#: manual/index.md:19
msgid "Every number in a report is recomputed from raw observations kept in the event stream; nothing is filtered or averaged before it is stored."
msgstr "报告中的每个数字都由保存在事件流中的原始观测重新计算；在存储之前不做任何过滤或平均。"

#: manual/index.md:21
msgid "Decisions compare paired deltas against a practical threshold stated in percent, and report the uncertainty next to the decision."
msgstr "决策把成对差值与以百分比表示的实际阈值进行比较，并在决策旁边报告不确定性。"

#: manual/index.md:23
msgid "Randomness is pinned by explicit seeds, so inputs, block orders and bootstrap intervals are reproducible on every target."
msgstr "随机性由显式的种子固定，因此输入、区组顺序和自助法区间在每个目标上都可复现。"

#: manual/index.md:26
msgid "Install"
msgstr "安装"

#: manual/index.md:32
msgid "Then import the packages you need in your `moon.pkg`, for example:"
msgstr "然后在你的 `moon.pkg` 中导入所需的包，例如："

#: manual/index.md:42
msgid "mare_mark needs the MoonBit toolchain 0.10 or later (`moonc` ≥ 0.10). It depends on `moonbitlang/x` 0.5.5 and `moonbitlang/async` 0.22.4. Every package compiles on all MoonBit targets. `runner.run` is asynchronous and runs where `moonbitlang/async` has a runtime: native, JS and wasm (not wasm-gc). Subprocess workers, the `replay` command and stdin/stdout reports need the native target."
msgstr "mare_mark 需要 MoonBit 工具链 0.10 或更高版本（`moonc` ≥ 0.10）。它依赖 `moonbitlang/x` 0.5.5 和 `moonbitlang/async` 0.22.4。每个包都能在所有 MoonBit 目标上编译。`runner.run` 是异步的，只能在 `moonbitlang/async` 提供运行时的地方运行：native、JS 和 wasm（不包括 wasm-gc）。子进程工作者、`replay` 命令以及 stdin/stdout 报告需要 native 目标。"

